IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, part sfad: Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (3), Debentures, ss 261 to 271 (lines 41833-42643 of SFA2001.txt).
-- Imports prelude, daydate, sfa-core and sfa-periods (every period is counted by sfa-periods, never here).
--
-- How to read a function in this module.
--   The result is MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE is yes on the facts; JUST FALSE is "the text says no in its own words";
--   NOTHING is "the text does not say" (silent, a list not closed, points outside the sources, limited by its own wording).
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every branch that answers "no" carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)` with the quoted words,
--   every branch that answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
--   A function named for what a provision REQUIRES ("must ...") answers JUST TRUE when the duty is on the person on the facts and
--   JUST FALSE when the text's own gate ("where", "if") is not met; whether the duty has been performed is a separate function.
--   Amounts, periods and thresholds the Act leaves to regulations, notices or the Authority are INPUTS.
--   "-- FORK" lines are collected into the fork register of NOTES.md; "-- SPLIT-SITE (i)" and "(ii)" mark the two open questions.

§ `Subdivision (3) Debentures: preliminary provisions, s 261`

-- src:41837 | 261.—(1) Subject to subsection (1A), this Subdivision applies
-- src:41838 | where an entity makes an offer of debentures.
@ref s 261(1) (src:41837-41838)
GIVEN
    `an entity makes an offer of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an entity make an offer of debentures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 261(1) this Subdivision applies to the offer` MEANS
    IF `an entity makes an offer of debentures`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this Subdivision applies where an entity makes an offer of debentures"
    -- FORK s261-1 | s 261(1) | `s 261(1) this Subdivision applies to the offer` | took JUST FALSE where the "where" gate fails | other reading NOTHING (a scope limit with no "only") | licence {P-b}; the other reading is {P-c}
    -- "Subject to subsection (1A)": the disapplication of ss 268, 269 and 270 is the next function, not a limit on this one.

-- src:41840 | (1A) Sections 268, 269 and 270 do not apply if the borrowing entity
-- src:41841 | is a prescribed entity.
@ref s 261(1A) (src:41840-41841)
GIVEN
    `the borrowing entity is a prescribed entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 261(1B) answer for the borrowing entity? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 261(1A) sections 268, 269 and 270 do not apply to the borrowing entity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the borrowing entity is a prescribed entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the borrowing entity is a prescribed entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply if the borrowing entity is a prescribed entity"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the borrowing entity's status as a prescribed entity is not known
    -- FORK s261-1A | s 261(1A) | `s 261(1A) sections 268, 269 and 270 do not apply to the borrowing entity` | took JUST FALSE where the "if" gate (prescribed entity) fails | other reading NOTHING ("if A then B" does not itself say "if not A then not B") | licence {IN-SHORT} (a condition introduced with "if") and the rule of 2026-10-29 (a)

-- src:41843 | (1B) In subsections (1A) and (1C), “prescribed entity” means —
-- src:41845 | (a) any bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970; or
-- src:41847 | (b) any entity or entity of a class which has been declared by
-- src:41848 | the Authority, by order in the Gazette, to be a prescribed
-- src:41849 | entity for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 261(1B) (src:41843-41849)
GIVEN
    `the entity is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970?
    `the Authority has declared the entity, or a class the entity is in, to be a prescribed entity for the purposes of section 261` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by order in the Gazette, declared the entity (or a class of entity it is in) to be a prescribed entity for the purposes of section 261?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 261(1B) the entity is a prescribed entity` MEANS
    IF `the entity is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` OR `the Authority has declared the entity, or a class the entity is in, to be a prescribed entity for the purposes of section 261`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“prescribed entity” means — (a) any bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970; or (b) any entity or entity of a class which has been declared by the Authority"

-- src:41851 | (1C) The Authority may, by written notice —
-- src:41853 | (a) impose such conditions or restrictions on a prescribed
-- src:41854 | entity as it thinks fit; and
-- src:41856 | (b) at any time vary or revoke any condition or restriction so
-- src:41857 | imposed,
-- src:41862 | and the prescribed entity must comply with every such condition or
-- src:41863 | restriction imposed on it by the Authority that has not been revoked
-- src:41864 | by the Authority.
@ref s 261(1C) (src:41851-41864)
GIVEN
    `the entity is a prescribed entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 261(1B) answer for the entity? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 261(1C)(a) the Authority may impose a condition or restriction on the entity` MEANS
    IF `the entity is a prescribed entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "impose such conditions or restrictions on a prescribed entity as it thinks fit"
    -- FORK s261-1Ca | s 261(1C)(a) | `s 261(1C)(a) the Authority may impose a condition or restriction on the entity` | took NOTHING where the entity is not (known to be) a prescribed entity | other reading JUST FALSE (the Authority may not) | licence {G1}: a function named for a power whose gate failed

@ref s 261(1C) (src:41856-41857)
GIVEN
    `a condition or restriction has been imposed on the entity by the Authority by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by written notice, imposed a condition or restriction on the entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 261(1C)(b) the Authority may vary or revoke the condition or restriction` MEANS
    IF `a condition or restriction has been imposed on the entity by the Authority by written notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "vary or revoke any condition or restriction so imposed"
    -- FORK s261-1Cb | s 261(1C)(b) | `s 261(1C)(b) the Authority may vary or revoke the condition or restriction` | took NOTHING where no condition has been imposed | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {G1}

@ref s 261(1C) (src:41862-41864)
GIVEN
    `the entity is a prescribed entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 261(1B) answer for the entity? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `a condition or restriction has been imposed on the entity by the Authority by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by written notice, imposed a condition or restriction on the entity?
    `the Authority has revoked the condition or restriction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority revoked the condition or restriction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 261(1C) the prescribed entity must comply with the condition or restriction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the entity is a prescribed entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `a condition or restriction has been imposed on the entity by the Authority by written notice` AND (NOT `the Authority has revoked the condition or restriction`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the entity is a prescribed entity` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the entity is a prescribed entity is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must comply with every such condition or restriction imposed on it by the Authority that has not been revoked"
    -- FORK s261-1C | s 261(1C) | `s 261(1C) the prescribed entity must comply with the condition or restriction` | took JUST FALSE where the condition was never imposed or has been revoked (a duty whose own gate is unmet) | other reading NOTHING (the class of conditions is limited by its own wording) | licence {G2} (a duty) and {CC} (a duty whose "if" or "where" is unmet)

-- src:41866 | (1D) Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction
-- src:41867 | imposed under subsection (1C)(a) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:41868 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in
-- src:41869 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding
-- src:41870 | $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence
-- src:41871 | continues after conviction.
@ref s 261(1D) (src:41866-41871)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (1C)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene a condition or restriction the Authority imposed on a prescribed entity under section 261(1C)(a)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 261(1D) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (1C)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction imposed under subsection (1C)(a) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
    -- FORK s261-1D | s 261(1D) | `s 261(1D) the person is guilty of an offence` | took JUST FALSE where the contravention element is unmet (this provision's own question: no contravention, no offence under it) | other reading NOTHING (the text does not say a person who has not contravened is not guilty of any offence) | licence {G2} ("the provision's own question") and the brief's split site (i)

@ref s 261(1D) (src:41866-41871)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 261(1D) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    -- fine not exceeding $50,000; no imprisonment (0 months); a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000

-- src:41875 | (3) In this Subdivision, a corporation is related to another
-- src:41876 | corporation if it is deemed to be related to that other corporation
-- src:41877 | by virtue of section 6 of the Companies Act 1967.
@ref s 261(3) (src:41875-41877)
GIVEN
    `the corporation is deemed to be related to the other corporation by virtue of section 6 of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation deemed to be related to the other corporation by virtue of section 6 of the Companies Act 1967?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 261(3) the corporation is related to the other corporation for this Subdivision` MEANS
    IF `the corporation is deemed to be related to the other corporation by virtue of section 6 of the Companies Act 1967`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a corporation is related to another corporation if it is deemed to be related to that other corporation by virtue of section 6 of the Companies Act 1967"
    -- FORK s261-3 | s 261(3) | `s 261(3) the corporation is related to the other corporation for this Subdivision` | took JUST FALSE where the "if" gate fails | other reading NOTHING (an "if" definition does not say "only if") | licence {IN-SHORT} ("if") and the rule of 2026-10-29 (a)

§ `s 262: offer of asset-backed securities`

-- src:41914 | “special purpose vehicle” means an entity that is established
-- src:41915 | solely in order to, or a trust that is established solely in order
-- src:41916 | for its trustee to, do either or both of the following:
-- src:41918 | (a) hold (whether as a legal or equitable owner) the
-- src:41919 | assets from which payments to holders of any
-- src:41920 | asset‑backed securities are or will be primarily
-- src:41921 | derived;
-- src:41923 | (b) issue any asset‑backed securities.
@ref s 262(3) "special purpose vehicle" (src:41914-41923)
GIVEN
    `the body is an entity established solely in order to hold the assets from which payments to holders of asset-backed securities are or will be primarily derived, or to issue asset-backed securities, or both` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body an entity (other than a trust) established solely in order to hold (as legal or equitable owner) the assets from which payments to holders of asset-backed securities are or will be primarily derived, or to issue asset-backed securities, or both?
    `the body is a trust established solely in order for its trustee to hold the assets from which payments to holders of asset-backed securities are or will be primarily derived, or to issue asset-backed securities, or both` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a trust established solely in order for its trustee to hold (as legal or equitable owner) the assets from which payments to holders of asset-backed securities are or will be primarily derived, or to issue asset-backed securities, or both?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 262(3) the body is a special purpose vehicle` MEANS
    IF `the body is an entity established solely in order to hold the assets from which payments to holders of asset-backed securities are or will be primarily derived, or to issue asset-backed securities, or both` OR `the body is a trust established solely in order for its trustee to hold the assets from which payments to holders of asset-backed securities are or will be primarily derived, or to issue asset-backed securities, or both`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“special purpose vehicle” means an entity that is established solely in order to, or a trust that is established solely in order for its trustee to, do either or both of the following"

-- src:41897 | “securitisation transaction” means an arrangement that involves
-- src:41898 | the sale, transfer or assignment of assets to a special purpose
-- src:41899 | vehicle where —
-- src:41901 | (a) such sale, transfer or assignment is funded by the
-- src:41902 | issue of debentures or units of debentures (whether
-- src:41903 | by that special purpose vehicle or another special
-- src:41904 | purpose vehicle); and
-- src:41909 | (b) payments in respect of such debentures or units of
-- src:41910 | debentures are or will be principally derived, directly
-- src:41911 | or indirectly, from the cash flows generated by the
-- src:41912 | assets;
@ref s 262(3) "securitisation transaction" (src:41897-41912)
GIVEN
    `the arrangement involves the sale, transfer or assignment of assets to a special purpose vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the arrangement involve the sale, transfer or assignment of assets to a special purpose vehicle?
    `the sale, transfer or assignment is funded by the issue of debentures or units of debentures, whether by that special purpose vehicle or another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sale, transfer or assignment funded by the issue of debentures or units of debentures (whether by that special purpose vehicle or another special purpose vehicle)?
    `payments in respect of the debentures or units of debentures are or will be principally derived, directly or indirectly, from the cash flows generated by the assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are payments in respect of those debentures or units of debentures, or will they be, principally derived (directly or indirectly) from the cash flows generated by the assets?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 262(3) the arrangement is a securitisation transaction` MEANS
    IF `the arrangement involves the sale, transfer or assignment of assets to a special purpose vehicle` AND `the sale, transfer or assignment is funded by the issue of debentures or units of debentures, whether by that special purpose vehicle or another` AND `payments in respect of the debentures or units of debentures are or will be principally derived, directly or indirectly, from the cash flows generated by the assets`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“securitisation transaction” means an arrangement that involves the sale, transfer or assignment of assets to a special purpose vehicle where"

-- src:41892 | (3) In this section —
-- src:41894 | “asset‑backed securities” means debentures or units of
-- src:41895 | debentures issued pursuant to a securitisation transaction;
@ref s 262(3) "asset-backed securities" (src:41892-41895)
GIVEN
    `the securities are debentures or units of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities debentures or units of debentures?
    `the securities are issued pursuant to a securitisation transaction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 262(3) "securitisation transaction" answer for the arrangement the securities are issued under? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 262(3) the securities are asset-backed securities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the securities are debentures or units of debentures`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“asset‑backed securities” means debentures or units of debentures issued pursuant to a securitisation transaction"
        IF `the securities are issued pursuant to a securitisation transaction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the securities are issued pursuant to a securitisation transaction` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "debentures or units of debentures issued pursuant to a securitisation transaction"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the arrangement is a securitisation transaction is not known

-- src:41881 | 262.—(1) An offer of asset‑backed securities is made only if they
-- src:41882 | are issued by —
-- src:41884 | (a) a special purpose vehicle other than a trust; or
-- src:41886 | (b) the trustee of a trust that is a special purpose vehicle.
@ref s 262(1) (src:41881-41886)
GIVEN
    `the securities are asset-backed securities` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 262(3) "asset-backed securities" answer for the securities? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the securities are issued by a special purpose vehicle other than a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities issued by a special purpose vehicle that is not a trust?
    `the securities are issued by the trustee of a trust that is a special purpose vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities issued by the trustee of a trust that is a special purpose vehicle?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 262(1) the asset-backed securities are issued by a special purpose vehicle or the trustee of one` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the securities are asset-backed securities` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An offer of asset‑backed securities is made only if"
        IF `the securities are asset-backed securities` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the securities are asset-backed securities is not known
        IF `the securities are issued by a special purpose vehicle other than a trust` OR `the securities are issued by the trustee of a trust that is a special purpose vehicle`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An offer of asset‑backed securities is made only if they are issued by"
    -- Read the question as "is the condition of the section met?": JUST TRUE is yes, and JUST FALSE is that the section bars the offer ("only if").

-- src:41888 | (2) The Authority may exempt any person or class of persons from
-- src:41889 | this section, subject to such conditions or restrictions as the Authority
-- src:41890 | may determine.
@ref s 262(2) (src:41888-41890)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has exempted the person or a class the person is in from section 262` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority exempted the person (or a class of persons the person is in) from section 262?
    `the person meets every condition or restriction the Authority determined for the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person meet every condition or restriction the Authority determined for the exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 262(2) the person is exempt from section 262` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has exempted the person or a class the person is in from section 262` AND `the person meets every condition or restriction the Authority determined for the exemption`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may exempt any person or class of persons from this section, subject to such conditions or restrictions as the Authority may determine"
    -- FORK s262-2 | s 262(2) | `s 262(2) the person is exempt from section 262` | took NOTHING where no exemption has been granted or a condition is unmet (a grant by the Authority) | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {G1}

§ `s 265: power of court in relation to certain irredeemable debentures`

-- src:41931 | 265.—(1) Despite anything in any debenture or trust deed, the
-- src:41932 | security for any debentures which are irredeemable or redeemable
-- src:41933 | only on the happening of a contingency is, if the court so orders,
-- src:41934 | enforceable, immediately or at such other time as the court directs if,
-- src:41935 | on the application of the trustee for the holders of the debentures or
-- src:41936 | (where there is no trustee) on the application of any holder of the
-- src:41937 | debentures, the court is satisfied that —
-- src:41939 | (a) at the time of the issue of the debentures the assets of the
-- src:41940 | borrowing entity which constituted or were intended to
-- src:41941 | constitute the security therefor were sufficient or likely to
-- src:41942 | become sufficient to discharge the principal debt and any
-- src:41943 | interest thereon;
-- src:41945 | (b) the security, if realised under the circumstances existing at
-- src:41946 | the time of the application, would be likely to bring not
-- src:41947 | more than 60% of the principal sum of moneys outstanding
-- src:41948 | (regard being had to all prior charges and charges ranking
-- src:41949 | pari passu, if any); and
-- src:41951 | (c) the assets covered by the security, on a fair valuation on the
-- src:41952 | basis of a going concern after allowing a reasonable
-- src:41957 | amount for depreciation are worth less than the principal
-- src:41958 | sum and the borrowing entity is not making sufficient
-- src:41959 | profit to pay the interest due on the principal sum or (where
-- src:41960 | no definite rate of interest is payable) interest thereon at
-- src:41961 | such rate as the court considers would be a fair rate to
-- src:41962 | expect from a similar investment.
@ref s 265(1) (src:41931-41962)
GIVEN
    `the debentures are irredeemable or redeemable only on the happening of a contingency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the debentures irredeemable, or redeemable only on the happening of a contingency?
    `the application is made by the trustee for the holders or, where there is no trustee, by a holder of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by the trustee for the holders of the debentures or, where there is no trustee, by a holder of the debentures?
    `at the time of the issue the assets that constituted or were intended to constitute the security were sufficient or likely to become sufficient to discharge the principal debt and any interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time the debentures were issued, were the assets of the borrowing entity that constituted or were intended to constitute the security sufficient, or likely to become sufficient, to discharge the principal debt and any interest on it?
    `the amount the security would be likely to bring if realised under the circumstances at the time of the application, after prior charges and charges ranking equally` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount would the security be likely to bring if realised under the circumstances existing at the time of the application, having regard to all prior charges and charges ranking equally (pari passu), in Singapore dollars?
    `the principal sum of moneys outstanding` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the principal sum of moneys outstanding, in Singapore dollars?
    `the assets covered by the security, on a fair valuation as a going concern after a reasonable allowance for depreciation, are worth less than the principal sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a fair valuation on the basis of a going concern, after a reasonable allowance for depreciation, are the assets covered by the security worth less than the principal sum?
    `the borrowing entity is not making sufficient profit to pay the interest due on the principal sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the borrowing entity not making sufficient profit to pay the interest due on the principal sum (or, where no definite rate is payable, interest at a rate the court considers fair)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 265(1) the court may order the security for the debentures to be enforceable` MEANS
    IF `the debentures are irredeemable or redeemable only on the happening of a contingency`
       AND `the application is made by the trustee for the holders or, where there is no trustee, by a holder of the debentures`
       AND `at the time of the issue the assets that constituted or were intended to constitute the security were sufficient or likely to become sufficient to discharge the principal debt and any interest`
       AND (`the amount the security would be likely to bring if realised under the circumstances at the time of the application, after prior charges and charges ranking equally` AT MOST (`the principal sum of moneys outstanding` TIMES 60%))
       AND `the assets covered by the security, on a fair valuation as a going concern after a reasonable allowance for depreciation, are worth less than the principal sum`
       AND `the borrowing entity is not making sufficient profit to pay the interest due on the principal sum`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is, if the court so orders, enforceable, immediately or at such other time as the court directs if, on the application of the trustee"
    -- JUST TRUE says the court may make the order; whether it does is the court's, and is not decided here.
    -- FORK s265-1 | s 265(1) | `s 265(1) the court may order the security for the debentures to be enforceable` | took NOTHING where a condition of the "if ... the court is satisfied" gate is unmet | other reading JUST FALSE (the court may not) | licence {G1}; "not more than 60%" is read as AT MOST 60% of the principal sum

-- src:41964 | (2) Subsection (1) does not affect any power to vary rights or accept
-- src:41965 | any compromise or arrangement created by the terms of the
-- src:41966 | debentures or the relevant trust deed or under a compromise or
-- src:41967 | arrangement between the borrowing entity and creditors.
@ref s 265(2) (src:41964-41967)
GIVEN
    `the power is created by the terms of the debentures or the relevant trust deed, or under a compromise or arrangement between the borrowing entity and creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the power to vary rights or to accept a compromise or arrangement created by the terms of the debentures or the relevant trust deed, or under a compromise or arrangement between the borrowing entity and creditors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 265(2) section 265(1) does not affect the power` MEANS
    IF `the power is created by the terms of the debentures or the relevant trust deed, or under a compromise or arrangement between the borrowing entity and creditors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not affect any power to vary rights or accept any compromise or arrangement created by the terms of the debentures"

§ `s 265A: requirement for trustees`

-- src:42072 | (5) In this section —
-- src:42074 | “asset‑backed securities” has the meaning given by
-- src:42075 | section 262(3);
-- src:42077 | “structured notes” has the meaning given by section 240AA(5).
@ref s 265A(5) (src:42072-42077)
GIVEN
    `the debentures are asset-backed securities as section 262(3) defines them` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 262(3) "asset-backed securities" answer for the debentures? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the notes are structured notes as section 240AA(5) defines them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the notes structured notes as section 240AA(5) defines them? (Section 240AA(5) is outside this encoding: answer from that section.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 265A(5) the debentures are asset-backed securities or structured notes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the debentures are asset-backed securities as section 262(3) defines them` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the notes are structured notes as section 240AA(5) defines them`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the debentures are asset-backed securities as section 262(3) defines them` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the debentures are asset-backed securities is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“asset‑backed securities” has the meaning given by section 262(3); “structured notes” has the meaning given by section 240AA(5)"

-- src:41971 | 265A.—(1) Where an offer of debentures is made in or
-- src:41972 | accompanied by a prospectus, the borrowing entity must appoint a
-- src:41973 | trustee for the holders of debentures (called in this section the
-- src:41974 | appointed trustee) for the entire tenure of the debentures.
@ref s 265A(1) (src:41971-41974)
GIVEN
    `an offer of debentures is made in or accompanied by a prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer of debentures made in, or accompanied by, a prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 265A(1) the borrowing entity must appoint a trustee for the holders of debentures for the entire tenure` MEANS
    IF `an offer of debentures is made in or accompanied by a prospectus`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offer of debentures is made in or accompanied by a prospectus, the borrowing entity must appoint a trustee"
    -- FORK s265A-1 | s 265A(1) | `s 265A(1) the borrowing entity must appoint a trustee for the holders of debentures for the entire tenure` | took JUST FALSE where the "where" gate fails | other reading NOTHING | licence {P-b} and {G2} (a duty); no deadline is stated, so the rule has no breach path

-- src:41978 | (2) The borrowing entity must ensure that —
-- src:41980 | (a) where the debentures are asset‑backed securities or
-- src:41981 | structured notes, the appointed trustee is any of the
-- src:41982 | following persons:
-- src:41984 | (i) a holder of a trust business licence under the Trust
-- src:41985 | Companies Act 2005 that is carrying on business in
-- src:41986 | Singapore in that capacity;
-- src:41988 | (ii) a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970 that is
-- src:41989 | carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity;
-- src:41991 | (iii) an approved trustee referred to in section 289 that is
-- src:41992 | carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity;
-- src:41994 | (iv) such other person as the Authority may prescribe by
-- src:41995 | regulations made under section 341;
-- src:41997 | (b) where the debentures are not asset‑backed securities or
-- src:41998 | structured notes, the appointed trustee is any of the
-- src:41999 | following persons:
-- src:42004 | (i) a holder of a trust business licence under the Trust
-- src:42005 | Companies Act 2005 that is carrying on business in
-- src:42006 | Singapore in that capacity;
-- src:42008 | (ii) a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970 that is
-- src:42009 | carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity;
-- src:42011 | (iii) an approved trustee referred to in section 289 that is
-- src:42012 | carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity;
-- src:42014 | (iv) any other person whom the borrowing entity is
-- src:42015 | satisfied, on reasonable grounds, is, and will be, able
-- src:42016 | to take timely and appropriate action on behalf of the
-- src:42017 | holders of debentures, in the event of a default or as
-- src:42018 | required by the trust deed;
-- src:42020 | (v) such other person as the Authority may prescribe by
-- src:42021 | regulations made under section 341;
-- src:42023 | (c) the appointed trustee is independent of the borrowing
-- src:42024 | entity, guarantor entity, arranger and counterparty of the
-- src:42025 | debentures; and
-- src:42027 | (d) the appointed trustee meets such requirements as the
-- src:42028 | Authority may prescribe by regulations made under
-- src:42029 | section 341.
@ref s 265A(2) (src:41978-42029)
GIVEN
    `the debentures are asset-backed securities or structured notes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 265A(5) answer for the debentures? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the appointed trustee is a holder of a trust business licence under the Trust Companies Act 2005 carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointed trustee a holder of a trust business licence under the Trust Companies Act 2005 that is carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity?
    `the appointed trustee is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970 carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointed trustee a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970 that is carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity?
    `the appointed trustee is an approved trustee referred to in section 289 carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointed trustee an approved trustee referred to in section 289 that is carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity?
    `the borrowing entity is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the appointed trustee is and will be able to take timely and appropriate action on behalf of the holders of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the borrowing entity satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the appointed trustee is, and will be, able to take timely and appropriate action on behalf of the holders of debentures in the event of a default or as required by the trust deed?
    `the appointed trustee is a person the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointed trustee a person the Authority has prescribed, by regulations made under section 341, for this purpose?
    `the appointed trustee is independent of the borrowing entity, the guarantor entity, the arranger and the counterparty of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointed trustee independent of the borrowing entity, the guarantor entity, the arranger and the counterparty of the debentures?
    `the appointed trustee meets the requirements the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the appointed trustee meet the requirements the Authority has prescribed, by regulations made under section 341, for this purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 265A(2) the borrowing entity has ensured that the appointed trustee meets the requirements` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the debentures are asset-backed securities or structured notes` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the debentures are asset-backed securities or structured notes is not known, so paragraph (a) or (b) cannot be chosen
        IF `the debentures are asset-backed securities or structured notes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN (IF ((`the appointed trustee is a holder of a trust business licence under the Trust Companies Act 2005 carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity` OR `the appointed trustee is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970 carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity` OR `the appointed trustee is an approved trustee referred to in section 289 carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity` OR `the appointed trustee is a person the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341`) AND `paragraphs (c) and (d) are met`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) where the debentures are asset‑backed securities or structured notes, the appointed trustee is any of the following persons"
        OTHERWISE (IF ((`the appointed trustee is a holder of a trust business licence under the Trust Companies Act 2005 carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity` OR `the appointed trustee is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970 carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity` OR `the appointed trustee is an approved trustee referred to in section 289 carrying on business in Singapore in that capacity` OR `the borrowing entity is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the appointed trustee is and will be able to take timely and appropriate action on behalf of the holders of debentures` OR `the appointed trustee is a person the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341`) AND `paragraphs (c) and (d) are met`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where the debentures are not asset‑backed securities or structured notes, the appointed trustee is any of the following persons"
    WHERE
        `paragraphs (c) and (d) are met` MEANS `the appointed trustee is independent of the borrowing entity, the guarantor entity, the arranger and the counterparty of the debentures` AND `the appointed trustee meets the requirements the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
    -- The text hands the prescribed persons and the prescribed requirements to regulations under section 341, which are not among the sources: they are inputs.
    -- FORK s265A-2 | s 265A(2) | `s 265A(2) the borrowing entity has ensured that the appointed trustee meets the requirements` | took JUST FALSE where the appointed trustee is none of the listed persons, or is not independent, or misses a prescribed requirement (the duty's own question) | other reading NOTHING (the list ends with a prescribed catch-all, so it is not closed by "only") | licence {G2} (a duty or the provision's own question)

-- src:42033 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2)(b)(iv), the borrowing entity
-- src:42034 | must, before being satisfied that a person is, and will be, able to take
-- src:42035 | timely and appropriate action on behalf of the holders of debentures,
-- src:42036 | in the event of a default or as required by the trust deed, consider the
-- src:42037 | following matters:
-- src:42039 | (a) whether the person is licensed or regulated in the
-- src:42040 | jurisdiction —
-- src:42042 | (i) in which the person was incorporated or formed; or
-- src:42044 | (ii) of the person’s principal place of business;
-- src:42046 | (b) the contractual arrangements between the borrowing entity
-- src:42047 | and the person;
-- src:42049 | (c) whether, if the person is the appointed trustee, the duties
-- src:42050 | which will be imposed on the person by way of the trust
-- src:42055 | deed, or under the laws and practices of the jurisdiction
-- src:42056 | referred to in paragraph (a), are at least equivalent to those
-- src:42057 | imposed under section 266(1);
-- src:42059 | (d) such other matters as the Authority may prescribe by
-- src:42060 | regulations made under section 341.
@ref s 265A(3) (src:42033-42060)
GIVEN
    `the borrowing entity has considered whether the person is licensed or regulated in the jurisdiction in which the person was incorporated or formed, or of the person's principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity considered whether the person is licensed or regulated in the jurisdiction in which the person was incorporated or formed, or of the person's principal place of business?
    `the borrowing entity has considered the contractual arrangements between the borrowing entity and the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity considered the contractual arrangements between itself and the person?
    `the person is the appointed trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the appointed trustee?
    `the borrowing entity has considered whether the duties imposed on the person are at least equivalent to those imposed under section 266(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity considered whether the duties imposed on the person by the trust deed, or under the laws and practices of the jurisdiction where the person is licensed or regulated, are at least equivalent to those imposed under section 266(1)?
    `the Authority has prescribed other matters by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed other matters, by regulations made under section 341, for the borrowing entity to consider?
    `the borrowing entity has considered the other matters the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity considered those other matters?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 265A(3) the borrowing entity has considered the matters before being satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the borrowing entity has considered whether the person is licensed or regulated in the jurisdiction in which the person was incorporated or formed, or of the person's principal place of business`
       AND `the borrowing entity has considered the contractual arrangements between the borrowing entity and the person`
       AND ((NOT `the person is the appointed trustee`) OR `the borrowing entity has considered whether the duties imposed on the person are at least equivalent to those imposed under section 266(1)`)
       AND ((NOT `the Authority has prescribed other matters by regulations made under section 341`) OR `the borrowing entity has considered the other matters the Authority has prescribed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the borrowing entity must, before being satisfied that a person is, and will be, able to take timely and appropriate action on behalf of the holders of debentures, in the event of a default or as required by the trust deed, consider the following matters"
    -- Paragraph (c) asks only "if the person is the appointed trustee"; paragraph (d) asks only for matters the Authority has prescribed.

-- src:42064 | (4) Any person who contravenes subsection (1), (2) or (3) shall be
-- src:42065 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:42066 | exceeding $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:42067 | further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:42068 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 265A(4) (src:42064-42068)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes section 265A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 265A(1) (by not appointing a trustee for the holders for the entire tenure)?
    `the person contravenes section 265A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 265A(2) (by not ensuring the appointed trustee meets the requirements)?
    `the person contravenes section 265A(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 265A(3) (by not considering the matters before being satisfied)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 265A(4) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes section 265A(1)` OR `the person contravenes section 265A(2)` OR `the person contravenes section 265A(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who contravenes subsection (1), (2) or (3) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
    -- FORK s265A-4 | s 265A(4) | `s 265A(4) the person is guilty of an offence` | took JUST FALSE where none of the three contraventions is shown (this provision's own question) | other reading NOTHING | licence {G2} and the brief's split site (i)

@ref s 265A(4) (src:42064-42068)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 265A(4) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    -- fine not exceeding $50,000; no imprisonment (0 months); a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000

§ `s 266: duties of trustees`

-- src:42083 | 266.—(1) A trustee for the holders of debentures must —
-- src:42085 | (a) at all times exercise due diligence and vigilance in carrying
-- src:42086 | out its functions and duties, and in safeguarding the rights
-- src:42087 | and interests of the holders of debentures;
-- src:42089 | (b) ensure that it has the ability and powers to perform all of its
-- src:42090 | duties as set out in the trust deed;
-- src:42092 | (c) ensure that any trustee appointed for the holders of any
-- src:42093 | collateral upon which the debentures are secured is subject
-- src:42094 | to duties that are at least equivalent to those imposed under
-- src:42095 | paragraphs (a) and (b); and
-- src:42097 | (d) comply with such other requirements as the Authority may
-- src:42098 | prescribe by regulations made under section 341, or as the
-- src:42099 | Authority may impose in respect of any particular offer or
-- src:42100 | transaction relating to the debentures.
@ref s 266(1) (src:42083-42100)
GIVEN
    `the trustee at all times exercises due diligence and vigilance in carrying out its functions and duties and in safeguarding the rights and interests of the holders of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee at all times exercise due diligence and vigilance in carrying out its functions and duties, and in safeguarding the rights and interests of the holders of the debentures?
    `the trustee has the ability and powers to perform all of its duties as set out in the trust deed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee have the ability and powers to perform all of its duties as set out in the trust deed?
    `any trustee appointed for the holders of collateral is subject to duties at least equivalent to those under paragraphs (a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any trustee appointed for the holders of any collateral on which the debentures are secured subject to duties at least equivalent to those imposed on the trustee under section 266(1)(a) and (b)? (Answer yes if there is no such trustee.)
    `there are other requirements the Authority has prescribed by regulations, or imposed for the particular offer or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed other requirements by regulations made under section 341, or imposed requirements for this particular offer or transaction relating to the debentures?
    `the trustee complies with those other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee comply with those other requirements?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266(1) the trustee for the holders of debentures has done what paragraphs (a) to (d) require` MEANS
    IF `the trustee at all times exercises due diligence and vigilance in carrying out its functions and duties and in safeguarding the rights and interests of the holders of the debentures`
       AND `the trustee has the ability and powers to perform all of its duties as set out in the trust deed`
       AND `any trustee appointed for the holders of collateral is subject to duties at least equivalent to those under paragraphs (a) and (b)`
       AND ((NOT `there are other requirements the Authority has prescribed by regulations, or imposed for the particular offer or transaction`) OR `the trustee complies with those other requirements`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trustee for the holders of debentures must — (a) at all times exercise due diligence and vigilance"

-- src:42107 | (2) Where, after due inquiry, the trustee for the holders of
-- src:42108 | debentures at any time is of the opinion that the assets of the
-- src:42109 | borrowing entity and of any of its guarantor entities which are or
-- src:42110 | should be available whether by way of security or otherwise, are
-- src:42111 | insufficient, or likely to become insufficient, to discharge the
-- src:42112 | principal debt as and when it becomes due, the trustee may apply
-- src:42113 | to the Authority for an order under this subsection.
@ref s 266(2) (src:42107-42113)
GIVEN
    `after due inquiry, the trustee is of the opinion that the assets of the borrowing entity and of its guarantor entities which are or should be available are insufficient, or likely to become insufficient, to discharge the principal debt as and when it becomes due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After due inquiry, is the trustee of the opinion that the assets of the borrowing entity and of any of its guarantor entities which are or should be available (by way of security or otherwise) are insufficient, or likely to become insufficient, to discharge the principal debt as and when it becomes due?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266(2) the trustee may apply to the Authority for an order` MEANS
    IF `after due inquiry, the trustee is of the opinion that the assets of the borrowing entity and of its guarantor entities which are or should be available are insufficient, or likely to become insufficient, to discharge the principal debt as and when it becomes due`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, after due inquiry, the trustee for the holders of debentures at any time is of the opinion that the assets of the borrowing entity"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
    -- FORK s266-2 | s 266(2) | `s 266(2) the trustee may apply to the Authority for an order` | took JUST FALSE where the "where" gate fails | other reading NOTHING (a grant limited by its own wording) | licence {P-b} (a "where ..." condition: when it fails the answer is JUST FALSE) against {IN-SHORT} (a grant limited in its own wording); {G3} says list it and do not change it

-- src:42115 | (3) The Authority, on such application —
-- src:42117 | (a) after giving the borrowing entity an opportunity of making
-- src:42118 | representations in relation to that application, by written
-- src:42119 | order served on the entity at its registered office in
-- src:42120 | Singapore, may impose such restrictions on the activities
-- src:42121 | of the borrowing entity, including restrictions on
-- src:42122 | advertising for deposits or loans and on borrowing by
-- src:42123 | the entity as the Authority thinks necessary for the
-- src:42124 | protection of the interests of the holders of the
-- src:42125 | debentures; or
@ref s 266(3)(a) (src:42115-42125)
GIVEN
    `an application has been made to the Authority under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trustee made an application to the Authority under section 266(2)?
    `the borrowing entity has been given an opportunity of making representations on the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity been given an opportunity of making representations on the application?
    `the order is in writing and served on the borrowing entity at its registered office in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order in writing and served on the borrowing entity at its registered office in Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266(3)(a) the Authority may impose restrictions on the activities of the borrowing entity` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made to the Authority under subsection (2)` AND `the borrowing entity has been given an opportunity of making representations on the application` AND `the order is in writing and served on the borrowing entity at its registered office in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after giving the borrowing entity an opportunity of making representations in relation to that application, by written order served on the entity at its registered office in Singapore, may impose such restrictions"
    -- FORK s266-3a | s 266(3)(a) | `s 266(3)(a) the Authority may impose restrictions on the activities of the borrowing entity` | took NOTHING where the application, the opportunity to make representations or the written order is missing | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {G1}

-- src:42127 | (b) may, and if the borrowing entity so requires, must direct
-- src:42128 | the trustee to apply to the court for an order under
-- src:42129 | subsection (5); and the trustee must apply accordingly.
@ref s 266(3)(b) (src:42127-42129)
GIVEN
    `an application has been made to the Authority under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trustee made an application to the Authority under section 266(2)?
    `the borrowing entity requires the Authority to direct the trustee to apply to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the borrowing entity require the Authority to direct the trustee to apply to the court for an order under section 266(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266(3)(b) the Authority must direct the trustee to apply to the court` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made to the Authority under subsection (2)` AND `the borrowing entity requires the Authority to direct the trustee to apply to the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, and if the borrowing entity so requires, must direct the trustee to apply to the court"
    -- Without the borrowing entity's requirement the Authority "may" direct, which is its discretion: the text does not say.

@ref s 266(3)(b) (src:42129-42129)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has directed the trustee to apply to the court for an order under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority directed the trustee to apply to the court for an order under section 266(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266(3)(b) the trustee must apply to the court as directed` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has directed the trustee to apply to the court for an order under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and the trustee must apply accordingly"
    -- FORK s266-3b | s 266(3)(b) | `s 266(3)(b) the trustee must apply to the court as directed` | took JUST FALSE where there is no direction (a duty whose gate "accordingly" is unmet) | other reading NOTHING | licence {CC} (a duty whose "if" or "where" is unmet) and {G2} (a duty)

-- src:42131 | (4) Where —
-- src:42133 | (a) after due inquiry, the trustee at any time is of the opinion
-- src:42134 | that the assets of the borrowing entity and of any of its
-- src:42135 | guarantor entities which are or should be available,
-- src:42136 | whether by way of security or otherwise, are insufficient
-- src:42137 | or likely to become insufficient, to discharge the principal
-- src:42138 | debt as and when it becomes due; or
-- src:42140 | (b) the borrowing entity has contravened an order made by the
-- src:42141 | Authority under subsection (2),
-- src:42143 | the trustee may, and where the borrowing entity has requested the
-- src:42144 | trustee to do so, must apply to the court for an order under
-- src:42145 | subsection (5).
@ref s 266(4) (src:42131-42145)
GIVEN
    `after due inquiry, the trustee is of the opinion that the assets of the borrowing entity and of its guarantor entities which are or should be available are insufficient, or likely to become insufficient, to discharge the principal debt as and when it becomes due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After due inquiry, is the trustee of the opinion that the assets of the borrowing entity and of any of its guarantor entities which are or should be available (by way of security or otherwise) are insufficient, or likely to become insufficient, to discharge the principal debt as and when it becomes due?
    `the borrowing entity has contravened an order made by the Authority under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity contravened an order made by the Authority (the text of section 266(4)(b) says "under subsection (2)")?
    `the borrowing entity has requested the trustee to apply to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity requested the trustee to apply to the court for an order under section 266(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266(4) the trustee may apply to the court for an order under subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF `after due inquiry, the trustee is of the opinion that the assets of the borrowing entity and of its guarantor entities which are or should be available are insufficient, or likely to become insufficient, to discharge the principal debt as and when it becomes due` OR `the borrowing entity has contravened an order made by the Authority under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where — (a) after due inquiry, the trustee at any time is of the opinion"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
    -- FORK s266-4a | s 266(4) | `s 266(4) the trustee may apply to the court for an order under subsection (5)` | took JUST FALSE where neither (a) nor (b) holds | other reading NOTHING | licence {P-b} against {IN-SHORT}; {G3}. Paragraph (b) speaks of an order "under subsection (2)"; subsection (2) itself says the trustee may apply "for an order under this subsection", while subsection (3) is where the Authority "by written order" imposes restrictions; the input is worded as the text words it (an order of the Authority on the application), and the numbering is recorded as finding F-266

@ref s 266(4) (src:42143-42145)
GIVEN
    `the trustee may apply to the court under subsection (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 266(4) answer for the trustee? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the borrowing entity has requested the trustee to apply to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity requested the trustee to apply to the court for an order under section 266(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266(4) the trustee must apply to the court for an order under subsection (5)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the trustee may apply to the court under subsection (4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the borrowing entity has requested the trustee to apply to the court`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the trustee may apply to the court under subsection (4)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the trustee may apply under subsection (4) is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the trustee may, and where the borrowing entity has requested the trustee to do so, must apply to the court for an order under subsection (5)"
    -- FORK s266-4b | s 266(4) | `s 266(4) the trustee must apply to the court for an order under subsection (5)` | took JUST FALSE where there is no request (a duty whose "where" gate is unmet) | other reading NOTHING | licence {CC} and {P-b}

-- src:42147 | (5) Where an application is made to the court under subsection (3)
-- src:42148 | or (4), the court may, after giving the borrowing entity an opportunity
-- src:42149 | to be heard, by order, do all or any of the following things:
-- src:42154 | (a) direct the trustee to convene a meeting of the holders of the
-- src:42155 | debentures for the purpose of placing before them such
-- src:42156 | information relating to their interests and such proposals
-- src:42157 | for the protection of their interests as the trustee considers
-- src:42158 | necessary or appropriate, and of obtaining their directions
-- src:42159 | in relation thereto and give such directions in relation to the
-- src:42160 | conduct of the meeting as the court thinks fit;
-- src:42162 | (b) stay all or any actions or proceedings before any court by
-- src:42163 | or against the borrowing entity;
-- src:42165 | (c) restrain the payment of any moneys by the borrowing
-- src:42166 | entity to the holders of debentures of the borrowing entity
-- src:42167 | or to any class of such holders;
-- src:42169 | (d) appoint a receiver of such of the property as constitutes the
-- src:42170 | security (if any) for the debentures;
-- src:42172 | (e) give such further directions from time to time as may be
-- src:42173 | necessary to protect the interests of the holders of the
-- src:42174 | debentures, the members of the borrowing entity or any of
-- src:42175 | its guarantor entities or the public,
-- src:42177 | but in making any such order the court must have regard to the rights
-- src:42178 | of all creditors of the borrowing entity.
@ref s 266(5) (src:42147-42178)
GIVEN
    `an application is made to the court under subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to the court under section 266(3) or (4)?
    `the borrowing entity has been given an opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity been given an opportunity to be heard?
    `the order directs a meeting of holders, stays proceedings, restrains payments, appoints a receiver or gives further directions to protect interests, as paragraphs (a) to (e) list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order one of the things listed in section 266(5)(a) to (e): convening a meeting of the holders, staying actions or proceedings against the borrowing entity, restraining payment of moneys to holders, appointing a receiver of the security, or giving further directions to protect the interests of the holders, the members of the borrowing entity or its guarantor entities, or the public?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266(5) the court may make the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `an application is made to the court under subsection (3) or (4)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application is made to the court under subsection (3) or (4), the court may"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
        IF `the borrowing entity has been given an opportunity to be heard` AND `the order directs a meeting of holders, stays proceedings, restrains payments, appoints a receiver or gives further directions to protect interests, as paragraphs (a) to (e) list`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after giving the borrowing entity an opportunity to be heard, by order, do all or any of the following things"
    -- FORK s266-5 | s 266(5) | `s 266(5) the court may make the order` | took JUST FALSE where there is no application ("where" gate) and NOTHING where the opportunity to be heard or the listed kind is missing | other reading NOTHING for the first and JUST FALSE for the second | licence {P-b} against {IN-SHORT} for the first; {G1} for the second; {G3}

@ref s 266(5) (src:42177-42178)
