    `the court has regard to the rights of all creditors of the borrowing entity in making the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court have regard to the rights of all creditors of the borrowing entity in making the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266(5) the court has done what it must in making the order` MEANS
    IF `the court has regard to the rights of all creditors of the borrowing entity in making the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but in making any such order the court must have regard to the rights of all creditors of the borrowing entity"

