-- src:42183 | (7) A trustee in making any application to the Authority or to the
-- src:42184 | court must have regard to the nature and kind of the security given
-- src:42185 | when the offer of the debentures was made, and if no security was
-- src:42186 | given must have regard to the position of the holders of the
-- src:42187 | debentures as unsecured creditors of the borrowing entity.
@ref s 266(7) (src:42183-42187)
GIVEN
    `the trustee is making an application to the Authority or to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trustee making an application to the Authority or to the court under section 266?
    `security was given when the offer of the debentures was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was security given when the offer of the debentures was made?
    `the trustee has regard to the nature and kind of the security given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee have regard to the nature and kind of the security given when the offer was made?
    `the trustee has regard to the position of the holders as unsecured creditors of the borrowing entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee have regard to the position of the holders of the debentures as unsecured creditors of the borrowing entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266(7) the trustee has had the regard the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the trustee is making an application to the Authority or to the court`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A trustee in making any application to the Authority or to the court must have regard"
        IF `security was given when the offer of the debentures was made`
        THEN (IF `the trustee has regard to the nature and kind of the security given` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have regard to the nature and kind of the security given when the offer of the debentures was made"
        OTHERWISE (IF `the trustee has regard to the position of the holders as unsecured creditors of the borrowing entity` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if no security was given must have regard to the position of the holders of the debentures as unsecured creditors of the borrowing entity"

