§ `ss 267 and 267A: the trustee, the holders, the Authority and the court`

-- src:42200 | 267.—(1) A trustee for the holders of debentures may apply to the
-- src:42201 | court —
-- src:42203 | (a) for directions in relation to any matter arising in connection
-- src:42204 | with the performance of the functions of the trustee; or
-- src:42206 | (b) to determine any question in relation to the interests of the
-- src:42207 | holders of debentures.
@ref s 267(1) (src:42200-42207)
GIVEN
    `the application is for directions in relation to a matter arising in connection with the performance of the functions of the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for directions in relation to a matter arising in connection with the performance of the trustee's functions?
    `the application is to determine a question in relation to the interests of the holders of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application to determine a question in relation to the interests of the holders of the debentures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267(1) the trustee for the holders of debentures may apply to the court` MEANS
    IF `the application is for directions in relation to a matter arising in connection with the performance of the functions of the trustee` OR `the application is to determine a question in relation to the interests of the holders of debentures`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may apply to the court — (a) for directions in relation to any matter arising in connection with the performance of the functions of the trustee; or (b) to determine any question in relation to the interests of the holders of debentures"
    -- FORK s267-1 | s 267(1) | `s 267(1) the trustee for the holders of debentures may apply to the court` | took NOTHING where the application is for neither purpose | other reading JUST FALSE (a list closed by "or") | licence {G1}

-- src:42209 | (2) The court may —
-- src:42211 | (a) give such directions to the trustee as the court thinks fit;
-- src:42212 | and
-- src:42214 | (b) if satisfied that the determination of the question will be
-- src:42215 | just and beneficial, accede wholly or partially to any such
-- src:42216 | application on such terms and conditions as the court
-- src:42217 | thinks fit or make such other order on the application as the
-- src:42218 | court thinks just.
@ref s 267(2) (src:42209-42218)
GIVEN
    `the application is made under section 267` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made to the court under section 267?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
