    IF `the application is made under section 267`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may — (a) give such directions to the trustee as the court thinks fit"
    -- Paragraph (a) is open to the court on any application under section 267; paragraph (b) is the next function.

@ref s 267(2)(b) (src:42214-42218)
GIVEN
    `the application is made under section 267` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made to the court under section 267?
    `the court is satisfied that the determination of the question will be just and beneficial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the determination of the question will be just and beneficial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267(2)(b) the court may accede to the application on terms or make another order` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under section 267` AND `the court is satisfied that the determination of the question will be just and beneficial`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if satisfied that the determination of the question will be just and beneficial, accede wholly or partially to any such application"
    -- FORK s267-2b | s 267(2)(b) | `s 267(2)(b) the court may accede to the application on terms or make another order` | took NOTHING where the court is not satisfied | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {G1}

