§ `s 268: obligations of borrowing entity`

-- s 268(1), (2) and (3) are each shown as [Deleted by Act 34 of 2012]: repealed rows in NOTES.md, no L4.

-- src:42255 | (4) Where there is a trustee for the holders of any debentures issued
-- src:42256 | by a borrowing entity, the borrowing entity and each of its guarantor
-- src:42257 | entities which has guaranteed the repayment of the moneys raised by
-- src:42258 | the issue of those debentures must, whether or not any demand
-- src:42259 | therefor has been made —
@ref s 268(4) (src:42255-42259)
GIVEN
    `there is a trustee for the holders of debentures issued by the borrowing entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a trustee for the holders of debentures issued by the borrowing entity?
    `the entity is the borrowing entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity the borrowing entity that issued the debentures?
    `the entity is a guarantor entity which has guaranteed the repayment of the moneys raised by the issue of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity a guarantor entity which has guaranteed the repayment of the moneys raised by the issue of the debentures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(4) the entity must provide the trustee with particulars of the charge` MEANS
    IF `there is a trustee for the holders of debentures issued by the borrowing entity` AND (`the entity is the borrowing entity` OR `the entity is a guarantor entity which has guaranteed the repayment of the moneys raised by the issue of the debentures`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is a trustee for the holders of any debentures issued by a borrowing entity, the borrowing entity and each of its guarantor entities which has guaranteed the repayment of the moneys raised by the issue of those debentures must"
    -- FORK s268-4 | s 268(4) | `s 268(4) the entity must provide the trustee with particulars of the charge` | took JUST FALSE where there is no trustee or the entity is neither the borrowing entity nor a guarantor (a duty whose "where" gate fails) | other reading NOTHING | licence {P-b} and {G2} (a duty)

-- src:42261 | (a) in writing provide the trustee, within 21 days after the
-- src:42262 | creation of the charge, with the particulars of any charge
-- src:42263 | created by the entity or the guarantor entity, as the case
-- src:42264 | requires; and
@ref s 268(4)(a) (src:42261-42264)
GIVEN
    `the day the charge was created` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the charge created?
    `the day the particulars are provided to the trustee` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the particulars provided to the trustee?
    `the particulars are provided in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the particulars provided in writing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(4)(a) the particulars of the charge are provided in time` MEANS
    IF `the particulars are provided in writing` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the charge was created` `the day the particulars are provided to the trustee` 21 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in writing provide the trustee, within 21 days after the creation of the charge, with the particulars of any charge"
    -- FORK s268-4a | s 268(4)(a) | `s 268(4)(a) the particulars of the charge are provided in time` | took JUST FALSE outside the 21 days or not in writing (a period fixed in the text's own words) | other reading NOTHING | licence {P-a}. The keel's convention P2 reads "within N days after" as a window that opens the day after the event; for a duty this encoding counts an act on or before the last day as in time ("not later than the end of"), so an early act is not late.

-- src:42266 | (b) when the amount to be advanced on the security of the
-- src:42267 | charge is indeterminate, in writing provide the trustee,
-- src:42268 | within 7 days after the advance, with particulars of the
-- src:42269 | amount or amounts in fact advanced.
@ref s 268(4)(b) (src:42266-42269)
GIVEN
    `the amount to be advanced on the security of the charge is indeterminate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount to be advanced on the security of the charge indeterminate?
    `the day of the advance` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the advance made?
    `the day the particulars of the amount advanced are provided to the trustee` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the particulars of the amount or amounts in fact advanced provided to the trustee?
    `the particulars are provided in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the particulars provided in writing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(4)(b) the particulars of the amounts advanced are provided in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the amount to be advanced on the security of the charge is indeterminate`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when the amount to be advanced on the security of the charge is indeterminate"
        IF `the particulars are provided in writing` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the advance` `the day the particulars of the amount advanced are provided to the trustee` 7 Days
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in writing provide the trustee, within 7 days after the advance, with particulars of the amount or amounts in fact advanced"

-- src:42271 | (5) Where any such advance referred to in subsection (4)(b) is
