-- src:42308 | (7A) Any person who contravenes subsection (6A) shall be guilty
-- src:42309 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:42310 | $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:42311 | both.
@ref s 268(7A) (src:42308-42311)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes subsection (6A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 268(6A)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(7A) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes subsection (6A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who contravenes subsection (6A) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
    -- FORK s268-7A | s 268(7A) | `s 268(7A) the person is guilty of an offence` | took JUST FALSE where the person does not contravene subsection (6A) | other reading NOTHING | licence {G2} and the brief's split site (i)

@ref s 268(7A) (src:42308-42311)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 268(7A) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    -- fine not exceeding $50,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years (24 months) or both; no continuing-offence fine (0)
    Penalty OF 50000, 24, TRUE, 0

-- src:42315 | (8) Sections 201(8), (9), (10), (12), (13), (14), (15), (15A) and (16)
-- src:42316 | and 207(1), (2) and (7) of the Companies Act 1967 are, with such
-- src:42317 | adaptations as are necessary, applicable to every profit and loss
-- src:42318 | account and balance sheet made out and lodged under subsection (6)
-- src:42319 | as if that profit and loss account and balance sheet were financial
-- src:42320 | statements referred to in those sections.
@ref s 268(8) (src:42315-42320)
GIVEN
    `the profit and loss account and balance sheet are made out and lodged under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the profit and loss account and balance sheet made out and lodged under section 268(6)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(8) the account and balance sheet are treated as financial statements for the Companies Act 1967 sections` MEANS
    IF `the profit and loss account and balance sheet are made out and lodged under subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "are, with such adaptations as are necessary, applicable to every profit and loss account and balance sheet made out and lodged under subsection (6)"
    -- What sections 201(8), (9), (10), (12), (13), (14), (15), (15A) and (16) and 207(1), (2) and (7) of the Companies Act 1967 then require is outside the sources.

-- src:42326 | (9) Where the directors or equivalent persons of a borrowing entity,
-- src:42327 | or the directors or equivalent persons of a guarantor entity, do not
-- src:42328 | lodge with the trustee the profit and loss accounts and balance sheets
-- src:42329 | as required under subsection (6) within the time prescribed under that
-- src:42330 | subsection, the trustee must immediately lodge notice of that fact
-- src:42331 | with the Authority.
@ref s 268(9) (src:42326-42331)
GIVEN
    `the directors or equivalent persons do not lodge the accounts with the trustee as required under subsection (6) within the time prescribed under that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors or equivalent persons of the borrowing entity or of the guarantor entity not lodged the profit and loss accounts and balance sheets with the trustee as section 268(6) requires, within the time that subsection prescribes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(9) the trustee must lodge notice of that fact with the Authority` MEANS
    IF `the directors or equivalent persons do not lodge the accounts with the trustee as required under subsection (6) within the time prescribed under that subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the directors or equivalent persons of a borrowing entity, or the directors or equivalent persons of a guarantor entity, do not lodge with the trustee the profit and loss accounts and balance sheets as required under subsection (6) within the time prescribed under that subsection, the trustee must immediately lodge notice"
    -- FORK s268-9 | s 268(9) | `s 268(9) the trustee must lodge notice of that fact with the Authority` | took JUST FALSE where the "where" gate fails | other reading NOTHING | licence {P-b} and {G2}. "Immediately" has no stated measure, so the rule has no breach path.

-- src:42335 | (10) Despite anything in subsection (8) —
-- src:42337 | (a) a profit and loss account and balance sheet of a borrowing
-- src:42338 | entity or its guarantor entity required to be made out and
-- src:42339 | lodged in accordance with subsection (6)(a) need not be
-- src:42340 | audited; and
@ref s 268(10)(a) (src:42335-42340)
GIVEN
    `the accounts are required to be made out and lodged in accordance with subsection (6)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the profit and loss account and balance sheet required to be made out and lodged in accordance with section 268(6)(a)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(10)(a) the half-year accounts need not be audited` MEANS
    IF `the accounts are required to be made out and lodged in accordance with subsection (6)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a profit and loss account and balance sheet of a borrowing entity or its guarantor entity required to be made out and lodged in accordance with subsection (6)(a) need not be audited"

-- src:42345 | (b) a profit and loss account and balance sheet of a borrowing
-- src:42346 | entity or its guarantor entity required to be made out and
-- src:42347 | lodged in accordance with subsection (6)(b) need not be
-- src:42348 | audited, or the audit thereof may be of a limited nature or
-- src:42349 | extent, if the trustee for the holders of the debentures of the
-- src:42350 | borrowing entity has, by written notice, consented to the
-- src:42351 | audit being dispensed with or being of a limited nature or
-- src:42352 | extent, as the case may be.
@ref s 268(10)(b) (src:42345-42352)
GIVEN
    `the accounts are required to be made out and lodged in accordance with subsection (6)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the profit and loss account and balance sheet required to be made out and lodged in accordance with section 268(6)(b)?
    `the trustee has, by written notice, consented to the audit being dispensed with or being of a limited nature or extent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trustee for the holders of the debentures, by written notice, consented to the audit being dispensed with or being of a limited nature or extent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(10)(b) the annual accounts need not be audited, or the audit may be limited` MEANS
    IF `the accounts are required to be made out and lodged in accordance with subsection (6)(b)` AND `the trustee has, by written notice, consented to the audit being dispensed with or being of a limited nature or extent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): without the trustee's consent subsection (8) applies the Companies Act 1967 sections, which are not among the sources
    -- FORK s268-10b | s 268(10)(b) | `s 268(10)(b) the annual accounts need not be audited, or the audit may be limited` | took NOTHING where there is no written consent (a relief limited by an "if", and what then applies is the Companies Act 1967) | other reading JUST FALSE (the audit is then required) | licence {G1} (a relief is read like a grant) against {IN-SHORT} ("if")

-- src:42356 | (11) Where the trustee has by written notice given the trustee’s
-- src:42357 | consent under subsection (10), the directors or equivalent persons of
-- src:42358 | the borrowing entity, or the directors or equivalent persons of the
-- src:42359 | guarantor entity, in respect of whose profit and loss account and
-- src:42360 | balance sheet the notice was given, must lodge with the Authority a
-- src:42361 | copy of the notice at the time when the profit and loss account and
-- src:42362 | balance sheet to which the notice relates are lodged with the
-- src:42363 | Authority.
@ref s 268(11) (src:42356-42363)
GIVEN
    `the trustee has by written notice given consent under subsection (10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trustee, by written notice, given consent under section 268(10)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(11) the directors or equivalent persons must lodge a copy of the notice with the Authority` MEANS
    IF `the trustee has by written notice given consent under subsection (10)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the trustee has by written notice given the trustee’s consent under subsection (10), the directors or equivalent persons of the borrowing entity, or the directors or equivalent persons of the guarantor entity, in respect of whose profit and loss account and balance sheet the notice was given, must lodge with the Authority a copy of the notice"
    -- FORK s268-11 | s 268(11) | `s 268(11) the directors or equivalent persons must lodge a copy of the notice with the Authority` | took JUST FALSE where there is no consent (a duty whose "where" gate fails) | other reading NOTHING | licence {P-b} and {CC}

@ref s 268(11) (src:42359-42363)
GIVEN
    `the day the accounts are lodged with the Authority` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the profit and loss account and balance sheet lodged with the Authority?
    `the day the copy of the notice is lodged with the Authority` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the copy of the trustee's notice lodged with the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(11) the copy of the notice is lodged at the time the accounts are lodged` MEANS
    IF `the day the copy of the notice is lodged with the Authority` EQUALS `the day the accounts are lodged with the Authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a copy of the notice at the time when the profit and loss account and balance sheet to which the notice relates are lodged with the Authority"
    -- FORK s268-11t | s 268(11) | `s 268(11) the copy of the notice is lodged at the time the accounts are lodged` | took "at the time when" to mean the same day (the clock here counts days) | other reading a same-moment test finer than a day | licence {P-a}

-- src:42365 | (12) Despite anything in this section, a profit and loss account and
-- src:42366 | balance sheet of a borrowing entity or its guarantor entity required to
-- src:42367 | be made out and lodged in accordance with subsection (6) may,
-- src:42368 | unless the trustee for the holders of the debentures of the borrowing
-- src:42369 | entity otherwise requires in writing, be based upon the value of the
-- src:42370 | stock in trade of the borrowing entity or the guarantor entity (as the
-- src:42371 | case may be) as reasonably estimated by the directors or equivalent
-- src:42372 | persons of the borrowing entity or guarantor entity.
@ref s 268(12) (src:42365-42372)
GIVEN
    `the accounts are required to be made out and lodged in accordance with subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the profit and loss account and balance sheet required to be made out and lodged in accordance with section 268(6)?
    `the trustee for the holders of the debentures otherwise requires in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee for the holders of the debentures otherwise require, in writing, that the stock in trade not be valued on the directors' estimate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(12) the accounts may be based on the directors' estimate of the stock in trade` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the accounts are required to be made out and lodged in accordance with subsection (6)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a profit and loss account and balance sheet of a borrowing entity or its guarantor entity required to be made out and lodged in accordance with subsection (6) may"
        IF `the trustee for the holders of the debentures otherwise requires in writing`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the trustee for the holders of the debentures of the borrowing entity otherwise requires in writing"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- FORK s268-12 | s 268(12) | `s 268(12) the accounts may be based on the directors' estimate of the stock in trade` | took JUST FALSE once the "unless" is met (the trustee requires otherwise in writing) | other reading NOTHING | licence {G2} ("may ... unless": the text closes the gate itself) and {CC} (an "unless" once it is met)

-- src:42374 | (13) The estimation of the directors or equivalent persons referred
-- src:42375 | to in subsection (12) must be made on the basis of the values of such
-- src:42376 | stock in trade as adopted for the purpose of the profit and loss account
-- src:42377 | and balance sheet of that entity laid before the entity at its last
-- src:42378 | preceding annual general meeting and certified in writing by the
-- src:42379 | directors or equivalent persons as such.
@ref s 268(13) (src:42374-42379)
GIVEN
    `the estimation is made on the basis of the values of stock in trade adopted for the accounts laid before the entity at its last preceding annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the directors' estimation made on the basis of the values of stock in trade adopted for the profit and loss account and balance sheet laid before the entity at its last preceding annual general meeting?
    `the values are certified in writing by the directors or equivalent persons as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those values certified in writing by the directors or equivalent persons as such?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(13) the estimation is made on the basis the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the estimation is made on the basis of the values of stock in trade adopted for the accounts laid before the entity at its last preceding annual general meeting` AND `the values are certified in writing by the directors or equivalent persons as such`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made on the basis of the values of such stock in trade as adopted for the purpose of the profit and loss account and balance sheet of that entity laid before the entity at its last preceding annual general meeting and certified in writing by the directors"

§ `s 268A: additional obligations of borrowing entity, where debentures are not listed on approved exchange`

-- src:42384 | 268A.—(1) A borrowing entity that issues any debentures which
-- src:42385 | are not listed on an approved exchange (called in this section unlisted
-- src:42386 | debentures) must, if the unlisted debentures have a tenure of
-- src:42391 | 12 months or longer, prepare and make available to the holders of the
-- src:42392 | debentures, in respect of the period of 6 months beginning on the date
-- src:42393 | of issuance of the debentures and each subsequent period of
-- src:42394 | 6 months, a report covering the period of 6 months (called in this
-- src:42395 | section a semi‑annual report), in accordance with this section and
-- src:42396 | such other requirements as the Authority may prescribe by
-- src:42397 | regulations made under section 341.
@ref s 268A(1) (src:42384-42397)
GIVEN
    `the borrowing entity issues debentures which are not listed on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the borrowing entity issue debentures which are not listed on an approved exchange?
    `the tenure of the unlisted debentures, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the tenure of the debentures, in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268A(1) the borrowing entity must prepare and make available a semi-annual report` MEANS
    IF `the borrowing entity issues debentures which are not listed on an approved exchange` AND (`the tenure of the unlisted debentures, in months` AT LEAST 12)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A borrowing entity that issues any debentures which are not listed on an approved exchange (called in this section unlisted debentures) must, if the unlisted debentures have a tenure of 12 months or longer, prepare and make available"
    -- FORK s268A-1 | s 268A(1) | `s 268A(1) the borrowing entity must prepare and make available a semi-annual report` | took JUST FALSE where the debentures are listed or the tenure is under 12 months (the "if" gate of a duty) | other reading NOTHING | licence {IN-SHORT} ("if") and {G2}. The form and content of the report are "such other requirements as the Authority may prescribe", outside the sources.

@ref s 268A(1) (src:42391-42397)
GIVEN
    `the date of issuance of the debentures` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the debentures issued?
    `the number of the period of 6 months, counting the period beginning on the date of issuance as 1` IS A NUMBER @desc Which period of 6 months is meant, counting the period of 6 months beginning on the date of issuance as 1?
GIVETH A DATE
`s 268A(1) the last day of the period of 6 months covered by a semi-annual report` MEANS
    IF `the number of the period of 6 months, counting the period beginning on the date of issuance as 1` AT MOST 1
    THEN `period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the date of issuance of the debentures` 6 Months
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period beginning with` ((`s 268A(1) the last day of the period of 6 months covered by a semi-annual report` `the date of issuance of the debentures` (`the number of the period of 6 months, counting the period beginning on the date of issuance as 1` MINUS 1)) PLUS 1) 6 Months
    -- The first period begins on the date of issuance; each later period begins the day after the one before it ends ("each subsequent period of 6 months").

-- src:42401 | (2) The borrowing entity must ensure that each semi‑annual report
-- src:42402 | covering a period of 6 months is lodged with the trustee for the
-- src:42403 | holders of the unlisted debentures, not later than 2 months after the
-- src:42404 | end of that period.
@ref s 268A(2) (src:42401-42404)
GIVEN
    `the last day of the period of 6 months` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period of 6 months the semi-annual report covers?
    `the day the semi-annual report is lodged with the trustee` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the semi-annual report lodged with the trustee for the holders of the unlisted debentures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268A(2) the semi-annual report is lodged with the trustee in time` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the last day of the period of 6 months` `the day the semi-annual report is lodged with the trustee` 2 Months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each semi‑annual report covering a period of 6 months is lodged with the trustee for the holders of the unlisted debentures, not later than 2 months after the end of that period"

-- src:42408 | (3) Where the borrowing entity does not lodge with the trustee for
-- src:42409 | the holders of unlisted debentures a semi‑annual report as required
-- src:42410 | under subsection (2), the trustee must immediately lodge notice of
-- src:42411 | that fact with the Authority.
@ref s 268A(3) (src:42408-42411)
GIVEN
    `the borrowing entity does not lodge with the trustee a semi-annual report as required under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the borrowing entity not lodge with the trustee for the holders of the unlisted debentures a semi-annual report as section 268A(2) requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268A(3) the trustee must lodge notice of that fact with the Authority` MEANS
    IF `the borrowing entity does not lodge with the trustee a semi-annual report as required under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the borrowing entity does not lodge with the trustee for the holders of unlisted debentures a semi‑annual report as required under subsection (2), the trustee must immediately lodge notice of that fact with the Authority"
    -- FORK s268A-3 | s 268A(3) | `s 268A(3) the trustee must lodge notice of that fact with the Authority` | took JUST FALSE where the "where" gate fails | other reading NOTHING | licence {P-b} and {G2}. "Immediately" has no stated measure, so the rule has no breach path.

-- src:42415 | (4) A borrowing entity must immediately disclose, in such form and
-- src:42416 | manner as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under
-- src:42417 | section 341, to holders of unlisted debentures any information which
-- src:42418 | may materially affect —
-- src:42420 | (a) the risks and returns of the unlisted debentures; or
-- src:42422 | (b) the price or value of the unlisted debentures.
@ref s 268A(4) (src:42415-42422)
GIVEN
    `the information may materially affect the risks and returns of the unlisted debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the information materially affect the risks and returns of the unlisted debentures?
    `the information may materially affect the price or value of the unlisted debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the information materially affect the price or value of the unlisted debentures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268A(4) the borrowing entity must disclose the information to the holders of unlisted debentures` MEANS
    IF `the information may materially affect the risks and returns of the unlisted debentures` OR `the information may materially affect the price or value of the unlisted debentures`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any information which may materially affect — (a) the risks and returns of the unlisted debentures; or (b) the price or value of the unlisted debentures"
    -- FORK s268A-4 | s 268A(4) | `s 268A(4) the borrowing entity must disclose the information to the holders of unlisted debentures` | took NOTHING for information that affects neither (a scope limit with no "only") | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {P-c}

@ref s 268A(4) (src:42415-42422)
GIVEN
    `the borrowing entity discloses the information to the holders immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the borrowing entity disclose the information to the holders of the unlisted debentures immediately?
    `the disclosure is in the form and manner the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure in the form and manner the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268A(4) the borrowing entity has disclosed the information as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the borrowing entity discloses the information to the holders immediately` AND `the disclosure is in the form and manner the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A borrowing entity must immediately disclose, in such form and manner as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under section 341, to holders of unlisted debentures any information"

-- src:42426 | (5) Any person who contravenes subsection (1), (2) or (4) shall be
-- src:42427 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:42428 | exceeding $20,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:42429 | further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:42430 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 268A(5) (src:42426-42430)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes section 268A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 268A(1)?
    `the person contravenes section 268A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 268A(2)?
    `the person contravenes section 268A(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 268A(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268A(5) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes section 268A(1)` OR `the person contravenes section 268A(2)` OR `the person contravenes section 268A(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who contravenes subsection (1), (2) or (4) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
    -- FORK s268A-5 | s 268A(5) | `s 268A(5) the person is guilty of an offence` | took JUST FALSE where none of the contraventions is shown | other reading NOTHING | licence {G2} and the brief's split site (i)

@ref s 268A(5) (src:42426-42430)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 268A(5) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    -- fine not exceeding $20,000; no imprisonment (0 months); a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction
    Penalty OF 20000, 0, FALSE, 2000

-- src:42434 | (6) Where the terms of any unlisted debentures provide for
-- src:42435 | redemption at the option of the holder of the unlisted debentures,
-- src:42436 | the borrowing entity must —
-- src:42438 | (a) make available bid or redemption prices of the unlisted
@ref s 268A(6) (src:42434-42438)
GIVEN
    `the terms of the unlisted debentures provide for redemption at the option of the holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms of the unlisted debentures provide for redemption at the option of the holder?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268A(6) the borrowing entity must make bid or redemption prices available and meet paragraphs (a) to (c)` MEANS
    IF `the terms of the unlisted debentures provide for redemption at the option of the holder`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the terms of any unlisted debentures provide for redemption at the option of the holder of the unlisted debentures, the borrowing entity must"
    -- FORK s268A-6 | s 268A(6) | `s 268A(6) the borrowing entity must make bid or redemption prices available and meet paragraphs (a) to (c)` | took JUST FALSE where the "where" gate fails | other reading NOTHING | licence {P-b} and {G2}

-- src:42438 | (a) make available bid or redemption prices of the unlisted
-- src:42439 | debentures, at the frequency at which the borrowing entity
-- src:42444 | has committed to buying back the unlisted debentures or
-- src:42445 | once every fortnight, whichever is more frequent, in such
-- src:42446 | form and manner as the Authority may prescribe by
-- src:42447 | regulations made under section 341;
@ref s 268A(6)(a) (src:42438-42447)
GIVEN
    `the borrowing entity has committed to a frequency of buying back the unlisted debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity committed to a frequency at which it will buy back the unlisted debentures?
    `the number of days between the buy-backs the borrowing entity has committed to` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are there between the buy-backs the borrowing entity has committed to? (Any number if it has made no commitment.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 268A(6)(a) the longest number of days allowed between times bid or redemption prices are made available` MEANS
    IF `the borrowing entity has committed to a frequency of buying back the unlisted debentures` AND (`the number of days between the buy-backs the borrowing entity has committed to` LESS THAN 14)
    THEN `the number of days between the buy-backs the borrowing entity has committed to`
    ELSE 14
    -- "whichever is more frequent": the shorter interval; "once every fortnight" is 14 days. The form and manner are the Authority's, by regulations made under section 341, outside the sources.

@ref s 268A(6)(a) (src:42438-42447)
GIVEN
    `the borrowing entity has committed to a frequency of buying back the unlisted debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity committed to a frequency at which it will buy back the unlisted debentures?
    `the number of days between the buy-backs the borrowing entity has committed to` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are there between the buy-backs the borrowing entity has committed to? (Any number if it has made no commitment.)
    `the number of days between the times the borrowing entity makes the prices available` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are there between the times the borrowing entity makes the bid or redemption prices available?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268A(6)(a) the bid or redemption prices are made available often enough` MEANS
    IF `the number of days between the times the borrowing entity makes the prices available` AT MOST (`s 268A(6)(a) the longest number of days allowed between times bid or redemption prices are made available` `the borrowing entity has committed to a frequency of buying back the unlisted debentures` `the number of days between the buy-backs the borrowing entity has committed to`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "make available bid or redemption prices of the unlisted debentures, at the frequency at which the borrowing entity has committed to buying back the unlisted debentures or once every fortnight, whichever is more frequent"

-- src:42449 | (b) if the published bid prices are indicative and may not be the
-- src:42450 | actual bid prices, clearly state this fact, wherever the
-- src:42451 | published bid prices appear, in such form and manner as
-- src:42452 | the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under
-- src:42453 | section 341; and
@ref s 268A(6)(b) (src:42449-42453)
GIVEN
    `the published bid prices are indicative and may not be the actual bid prices` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the published bid prices indicative, so that they may not be the actual bid prices?
    `the borrowing entity clearly states this fact wherever the published bid prices appear, in the form and manner prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the borrowing entity clearly state this fact wherever the published bid prices appear, in the form and manner the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268A(6)(b) the indicative bid prices are clearly stated to be indicative` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the published bid prices are indicative and may not be the actual bid prices`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the published bid prices are indicative and may not be the actual bid prices, clearly state this fact"
        IF `the borrowing entity clearly states this fact wherever the published bid prices appear, in the form and manner prescribed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "clearly state this fact, wherever the published bid prices appear"

-- src:42455 | (c) ensure that the bid or redemption prices are determined in
-- src:42456 | an independent and fair manner.
@ref s 268A(6)(c) (src:42455-42456)
GIVEN
    `the bid or redemption prices are determined in an independent and fair manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the bid or redemption prices determined in an independent and fair manner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268A(6)(c) the bid or redemption prices are determined in an independent and fair manner` MEANS
    IF `the bid or redemption prices are determined in an independent and fair manner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ensure that the bid or redemption prices are determined in an independent and fair manner"

-- src:42460 | (7) A borrowing entity must ensure that each profit and loss account
-- src:42461 | or balance sheet that its directors or equivalent persons are required to
-- src:42462 | lodge under section 268(6) is made available, in such form and
-- src:42463 | manner as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under
-- src:42464 | section 341, to holders of unlisted debentures, on the day of lodgment
-- src:42465 | of the profit and loss account or balance sheet (as the case may be)
-- src:42466 | with the trustee for the holders of the unlisted debentures.
@ref s 268A(7) (src:42460-42466)
GIVEN
    `the day the accounts are lodged with the trustee` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the profit and loss account and balance sheet lodged with the trustee for the holders of the unlisted debentures?
    `the day the accounts are made available to the holders` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the profit and loss account and balance sheet made available to the holders of the unlisted debentures?
    `the accounts are made available in the form and manner the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the accounts made available in the form and manner the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268A(7) the accounts are made available to the holders on the day of lodgment` MEANS
    IF (`the day the accounts are made available to the holders` EQUALS `the day the accounts are lodged with the trustee`) AND `the accounts are made available in the form and manner the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is made available, in such form and manner as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under section 341, to holders of unlisted debentures, on the day of lodgment of the profit and loss account or balance sheet"

-- src:42470 | (8) Any person who contravenes subsection (6) or (7) shall be
-- src:42471 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:42472 | exceeding $15,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
