§ `s 269: obligation of guarantor entity to provide information`

-- src:42497 | 269.—(1) For the purpose of the preparation of a report that, by this
-- src:42498 | Subdivision, is required to be signed by or on behalf of the directors
-- src:42499 | or equivalent persons, or persons approved by the Authority, of a
-- src:42500 | borrowing entity or any of them, that borrowing entity may, by
-- src:42501 | written notice, require any of its guarantor entities to provide it with
-- src:42502 | any information relating to that guarantor entity which is, by this
-- src:42503 | Subdivision, required to be contained in that report.
@ref s 269(1) (src:42497-42503)
GIVEN
    `the report is one this Subdivision requires to be signed by or on behalf of the directors or equivalent persons, or persons approved by the Authority, of the borrowing entity or any of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the report one that this Subdivision requires to be signed by or on behalf of the directors or equivalent persons (or persons approved by the Authority) of the borrowing entity, or any of them?
    `the entity is a guarantor entity of the borrowing entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity a guarantor entity of the borrowing entity?
    `the information relates to the guarantor entity and this Subdivision requires it to be contained in the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information information relating to the guarantor entity that this Subdivision requires to be contained in the report?
    `the requirement is made by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by written notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269(1) the borrowing entity may require the guarantor entity to provide the information` MEANS
    IF `the report is one this Subdivision requires to be signed by or on behalf of the directors or equivalent persons, or persons approved by the Authority, of the borrowing entity or any of them` AND `the entity is a guarantor entity of the borrowing entity` AND `the information relates to the guarantor entity and this Subdivision requires it to be contained in the report` AND `the requirement is made by written notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that borrowing entity may, by written notice, require any of its guarantor entities to provide it with any information relating to that guarantor entity which is, by this Subdivision, required to be contained in that report"
    -- FORK s269-1 | s 269(1) | `s 269(1) the borrowing entity may require the guarantor entity to provide the information` | took NOTHING where a limb of the power is missing | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {G1}

-- src:42505 | (2) The guarantor entity must provide the borrowing entity with the
-- src:42506 | information required under subsection (1) before such date, being a
-- src:42507 | date not earlier than 14 days after the notice is given, as may be
-- src:42508 | specified in that behalf in the notice.
@ref s 269(2) (src:42505-42508)
GIVEN
    `the borrowing entity has required the information by written notice under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity, by written notice under section 269(1), required the guarantor entity to provide the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269(2) the guarantor entity must provide the borrowing entity with the information` MEANS
    IF `the borrowing entity has required the information by written notice under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The guarantor entity must provide the borrowing entity with the information required under subsection (1)"
    -- FORK s269-2 | s 269(2) | `s 269(2) the guarantor entity must provide the borrowing entity with the information` | took JUST FALSE where no notice under subsection (1) has been given (the duty is of "the information required under subsection (1)") | other reading NOTHING | licence {G2} (a duty) and {CC}

@ref s 269(2) (src:42505-42508)
GIVEN
    `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice given?
    `the date specified in the notice` IS A DATE @desc What date does the notice specify for the information to be provided before?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269(2) the date specified in the notice is not earlier than 14 days after the notice is given` MEANS
    IF `the date specified in the notice` AT LEAST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the notice is given` 14 Days)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before such date, being a date not earlier than 14 days after the notice is given"

@ref s 269(2) (src:42505-42508)
GIVEN
    `the date specified in the notice` IS A DATE @desc What date does the notice specify for the information to be provided before?
    `the day the information is provided` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the information provided to the borrowing entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269(2) the information is provided before the date specified in the notice` MEANS
    IF `the day the information is provided` LESS THAN `the date specified in the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must provide the borrowing entity with the information required under subsection (1) before such date"
    -- FORK s269-2t | s 269(2) | `s 269(2) the information is provided before the date specified in the notice` | took "before such date" to exclude the specified date itself, so the last day to provide is the day before it | other reading the specified date is itself in time | licence {P-a}

-- src:42510 | (3) A guarantor entity which fails to comply with a requirement
-- src:42511 | contained in a notice given under subsection (1) and every officer or
-- src:42512 | equivalent person of that entity who is in default shall be guilty of an
-- src:42513 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:42514 | $20,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:42515 | exceeding $2,000 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:42516 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 269(3) (src:42510-42516)
GIVEN
    `the guarantor entity fails to comply with a requirement contained in a notice given under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the guarantor entity fail to comply with a requirement contained in a notice given under section 269(1)?
    `the person is the guarantor entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the guarantor entity?
    `the person is an officer or equivalent person of the guarantor entity who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer or equivalent person of the guarantor entity who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269(3) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the guarantor entity fails to comply with a requirement contained in a notice given under subsection (1)` AND (`the person is the guarantor entity` OR `the person is an officer or equivalent person of the guarantor entity who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A guarantor entity which fails to comply with a requirement contained in a notice given under subsection (1) and every officer or equivalent person of that entity who is in default shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
    -- FORK s269-3 | s 269(3) | `s 269(3) the person is guilty of an offence` | took JUST FALSE where the entity has not failed, or the person is neither the entity nor an officer in default | other reading NOTHING | licence {G2} and the brief's split site (i)

@ref s 269(3) (src:42510-42516)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 269(3) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    -- fine not exceeding $20,000; no imprisonment (0 months); a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction
    Penalty OF 20000, 0, FALSE, 2000

§ `s 270: loans and deposits to be immediately repayable on certain events`

-- src:42521 | 270.—(1) Where there is, in any prospectus issued in connection
-- src:42522 | with an offer of debentures, a statement as to any particular purpose
-- src:42523 | or project for which the moneys received by the borrowing entity in
-- src:42524 | response to the offer are to be applied, the borrowing entity must,
-- src:42525 | where there is a trustee for the holders of those debentures, from time
-- src:42526 | to time make reports to the trustee as to the progress that has been
-- src:42527 | made towards achieving such purpose or completing such project.
@ref s 270(1) (src:42521-42527)
GIVEN
    `a prospectus issued in connection with the offer of debentures states a particular purpose or project for which the moneys received in response to the offer are to be applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a prospectus issued in connection with the offer of debentures state a particular purpose or project for which the moneys received by the borrowing entity in response to the offer are to be applied?
    `there is a trustee for the holders of those debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a trustee for the holders of those debentures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(1) the borrowing entity must make reports to the trustee on the progress of the purpose or project` MEANS
    IF `a prospectus issued in connection with the offer of debentures states a particular purpose or project for which the moneys received in response to the offer are to be applied` AND `there is a trustee for the holders of those debentures`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is, in any prospectus issued in connection with an offer of debentures, a statement as to any particular purpose or project for which the moneys received by the borrowing entity in response to the offer are to be applied, the borrowing entity must, where there is a trustee"
    -- FORK s270-1 | s 270(1) | `s 270(1) the borrowing entity must make reports to the trustee on the progress of the purpose or project` | took JUST FALSE where a "where" gate fails | other reading NOTHING | licence {P-b} and {G2}. "From time to time" states no period, so the rule has no breach path.

-- src:42529 | (2) Each such report must be included in the report required to be
-- src:42530 | provided to the trustee for the holders of the debentures under
-- src:42531 | section 268(1).
@ref s 270(2) (src:42529-42531)
GIVEN
    `the progress report is included in the report to be provided to the trustee under section 268(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each progress report included in the report that is to be provided to the trustee under section 268(1)? (Section 268(1) is shown as deleted: see NOTES.md.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(2) the progress report is included in the report required under section 268(1)` MEANS
    IF `the progress report is included in the report to be provided to the trustee under section 268(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Each such report must be included in the report required to be provided to the trustee for the holders of the debentures under section 268(1)"
    -- Section 268(1) is shown in this text as [Deleted by Act 34 of 2012]: the text points at a report that no longer has a provision. The function asks the fact as the text words it.

-- src:42533 | (3) When it appears to the trustee for the holders of the debentures
-- src:42534 | that such purpose or project has not been achieved or completed —
-- src:42539 | (a) within the time stated in the prospectus within which the
-- src:42540 | purpose or project is to be achieved or completed; or
-- src:42542 | (b) where no such time was stated, within a reasonable time,
-- src:42544 | the trustee may and, if in the trustee’s opinion it is necessary for the
-- src:42545 | protection of the interests of the holders of the debentures, must give
-- src:42546 | written notice to the borrowing entity requiring it to repay the moneys
-- src:42547 | so received by the borrowing entity and, within one month after such
-- src:42548 | notice is given, lodge with the Authority a copy thereof.
@ref s 270(3) (src:42533-42548)
GIVEN
    `a time was stated in the prospectus within which the purpose or project is to be achieved or completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the prospectus state a time within which the purpose or project is to be achieved or completed?
    `it appears to the trustee that the purpose or project has not been achieved or completed within the time stated in the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the trustee that the purpose or project has not been achieved or completed within the time stated in the prospectus?
    `it appears to the trustee that the purpose or project has not been achieved or completed within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the trustee that the purpose or project has not been achieved or completed within a reasonable time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(3) the trustee may give written notice requiring the borrowing entity to repay the moneys` MEANS
    IF (`a time was stated in the prospectus within which the purpose or project is to be achieved or completed` AND `it appears to the trustee that the purpose or project has not been achieved or completed within the time stated in the prospectus`) OR ((NOT `a time was stated in the prospectus within which the purpose or project is to be achieved or completed`) AND `it appears to the trustee that the purpose or project has not been achieved or completed within a reasonable time`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When it appears to the trustee for the holders of the debentures that such purpose or project has not been achieved or completed"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
    -- FORK s270-3 | s 270(3) | `s 270(3) the trustee may give written notice requiring the borrowing entity to repay the moneys` | took JUST FALSE where the "when" gate fails | other reading NOTHING (a grant limited by its own wording) | licence {DEF-c} ("when" counts as "where" under rule (b) of the periods ruling) against {IN-SHORT}; {G3}

@ref s 270(3) (src:42544-42548)
GIVEN
    `the trustee may give notice under subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 270(3) "may give written notice" answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `in the trustee's opinion it is necessary for the protection of the interests of the holders of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the trustee's opinion, is it necessary for the protection of the interests of the holders of the debentures to give the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(3) the trustee must give written notice requiring the borrowing entity to repay the moneys` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the trustee may give notice under subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `in the trustee's opinion it is necessary for the protection of the interests of the holders of the debentures`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the trustee may give notice under subsection (3)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the trustee may give notice is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the trustee may and, if in the trustee’s opinion it is necessary for the protection of the interests of the holders of the debentures, must give written notice"

@ref s 270(3) (src:42544-42548)
GIVEN
    `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice given to the borrowing entity?
    `the day the copy of the notice is lodged with the Authority` IS A DATE @desc On what day was a copy of the notice lodged with the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(3) the copy of the notice is lodged with the Authority in time` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the notice is given` `the day the copy of the notice is lodged with the Authority` 1 Months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and, within one month after such notice is given, lodge with the Authority a copy thereof"

-- src:42550 | (4) The trustee must not give notice under subsection (3) if the
-- src:42551 | trustee is satisfied —
-- src:42553 | (a) that the purpose or project has been substantially achieved
-- src:42554 | or completed;
-- src:42556 | (b) that the interests of the holders of debentures have not been
-- src:42557 | materially prejudiced by the failure to achieve or complete
-- src:42558 | the purpose or project within the time stated in the
-- src:42559 | prospectus or within a reasonable time; or
-- src:42561 | (c) that the failure to achieve the purpose or project was due to
-- src:42562 | circumstances beyond the control of the borrowing entity
-- src:42563 | that could not reasonably have been foreseen by the
-- src:42564 | borrowing entity at the time that the prospectus was issued.
@ref s 270(4) (src:42550-42564)
GIVEN
    `the trustee is satisfied that the purpose or project has been substantially achieved or completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trustee satisfied that the purpose or project has been substantially achieved or completed?
    `the trustee is satisfied that the interests of the holders have not been materially prejudiced by the failure to achieve or complete the purpose or project in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trustee satisfied that the interests of the holders of the debentures have not been materially prejudiced by the failure to achieve or complete the purpose or project within the time stated in the prospectus or within a reasonable time?
    `the trustee is satisfied that the failure was due to circumstances beyond the control of the borrowing entity that could not reasonably have been foreseen when the prospectus was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trustee satisfied that the failure to achieve the purpose or project was due to circumstances beyond the control of the borrowing entity that could not reasonably have been foreseen by it when the prospectus was issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(4) the trustee must not give notice under subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `the trustee is satisfied that the purpose or project has been substantially achieved or completed` OR `the trustee is satisfied that the interests of the holders have not been materially prejudiced by the failure to achieve or complete the purpose or project in time` OR `the trustee is satisfied that the failure was due to circumstances beyond the control of the borrowing entity that could not reasonably have been foreseen when the prospectus was issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The trustee must not give notice under subsection (3) if the trustee is satisfied"
    -- FORK s270-4 | s 270(4) | `s 270(4) the trustee must not give notice under subsection (3)` | took JUST FALSE where the trustee is satisfied of none of (a) to (c) (a bar whose "if" gate is unmet: the bar does not apply) | other reading NOTHING (a prohibition limited by its own wording, case outside the limit) | licence {G2} (a bar) against {IN-SHORT}

-- src:42566 | (5) Upon receipt by the borrowing entity of a notice referred to in
-- src:42567 | subsection (3), the borrowing entity is liable to repay, and on demand
-- src:42568 | in writing by a person entitled thereto must immediately repay to the
-- src:42569 | person any moneys owing to the person as the result of a loan or
-- src:42570 | deposit made in response to the offer unless —
-- src:42572 | (a) before the moneys were accepted by the borrowing entity,
-- src:42573 | the borrowing entity had given written notice to the
-- src:42574 | persons from whom the moneys were received specifying
-- src:42575 | the purpose or project for which the moneys would in fact
-- src:42576 | be used and the moneys were accepted by the borrowing
-- src:42577 | entity accordingly; or
-- src:42579 | (b) the borrowing entity by written notice served on the
-- src:42580 | holders of the debentures —
-- src:42585 | (i) had specified the purpose or project for which the
-- src:42586 | moneys would in fact be applied by the borrowing
-- src:42587 | entity; and
-- src:42589 | (ii) had offered to repay the moneys to the holders of the
-- src:42590 | debentures, and that person had not within 14 days
-- src:42591 | after the receipt of the notice, or such longer time as
-- src:42592 | was specified in the notice, in writing demanded
-- src:42593 | from the borrowing entity repayment of the money.
@ref s 270(5) (src:42566-42593)
GIVEN
    `the borrowing entity has received a notice referred to in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity received a notice referred to in section 270(3)?
    `the moneys are owing to the person as the result of a loan or deposit made in response to the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the moneys owing to the person as the result of a loan or deposit made in response to the offer?
    `before the moneys were accepted the borrowing entity gave written notice to the persons the moneys were received from specifying the purpose or project, and accepted the moneys accordingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before the moneys were accepted, did the borrowing entity give written notice to the persons from whom the moneys were received specifying the purpose or project for which the moneys would in fact be used, and did it accept the moneys accordingly?
    `by written notice served on the holders the borrowing entity specified the purpose or project for which the moneys would in fact be applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By written notice served on the holders of the debentures, did the borrowing entity specify the purpose or project for which the moneys would in fact be applied?
    `by that notice the borrowing entity offered to repay the moneys to the holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By that notice, did the borrowing entity offer to repay the moneys to the holders of the debentures?
    `the person demanded repayment from the borrowing entity in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person demand repayment from the borrowing entity in writing?
    `the day the person received the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person receive the borrowing entity's notice?
    `the day the person demanded repayment in writing` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person demand repayment in writing? (Any date if the person did not.)
    `the longer time specified in the notice, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc If the notice specified a time longer than 14 days to demand repayment, how many days? (0 if it specified none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(5) the borrowing entity is liable to repay the moneys` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the borrowing entity has received a notice referred to in subsection (3)`) OR (NOT `the moneys are owing to the person as the result of a loan or deposit made in response to the offer`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon receipt by the borrowing entity of a notice referred to in subsection (3), the borrowing entity is liable to repay"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
        IF `before the moneys were accepted the borrowing entity gave written notice to the persons the moneys were received from specifying the purpose or project, and accepted the moneys accordingly`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless — (a) before the moneys were accepted by the borrowing entity, the borrowing entity had given written notice to the persons from whom the moneys were received specifying the purpose or project for which the moneys would in fact be used"
        IF `by written notice served on the holders the borrowing entity specified the purpose or project for which the moneys would in fact be applied` AND `by that notice the borrowing entity offered to repay the moneys to the holders` AND ((NOT `the person demanded repayment from the borrowing entity in writing`) OR (`the day the person demanded repayment in writing` GREATER THAN (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the person received the notice` (IF `the longer time specified in the notice, in days` GREATER THAN 14 THEN `the longer time specified in the notice, in days` ELSE 14) Days)))
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the borrowing entity by written notice served on the holders of the debentures — (i) had specified the purpose or project for which the moneys would in fact be applied by the borrowing entity; and (ii) had offered to repay the moneys to the holders of the debentures"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- FORK s270-5a | s 270(5) | `s 270(5) the borrowing entity is liable to repay the moneys` | took JUST FALSE once the "unless" is met (paragraph (a), or paragraph (b) with no demand in time) | other reading NOTHING | licence {G2} ("unless") and {CC} (an "unless" once it is met)
    -- FORK s270-5b | s 270(5) | the same function, "Upon receipt ... of a notice" | took JUST FALSE where there is no notice or no moneys owing ("upon" counts as "where") | other reading NOTHING | licence {DEF-c} against {IN-SHORT}; {G3} does not apply because the function is named for a liability, not a power
    -- The 14 days run from the receipt of the notice, or "such longer time as was specified in the notice"; the person's demand is in time if made on or before the last day. "On demand in writing ... must immediately repay" states no period, so the rule has no breach path.

-- src:42595 | (6) Where the borrowing entity has given written notice as provided
-- src:42596 | in subsection (5), specifying the purpose or project for which the
-- src:42597 | moneys will in fact be applied by the borrowing entity, this section
-- src:42598 | applies and has effect as if the purpose or project so specified in the
-- src:42599 | notice was the particular purpose or project specified in the
-- src:42600 | prospectus as the purpose or project for which the moneys were to
-- src:42601 | be applied.
@ref s 270(6) (src:42595-42601)
GIVEN
    `the borrowing entity has given written notice as provided in subsection (5) specifying the purpose or project for which the moneys will in fact be applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the borrowing entity given written notice as provided in section 270(5), specifying the purpose or project for which the moneys will in fact be applied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(6) the purpose in the notice is treated as the purpose specified in the prospectus` MEANS
    IF `the borrowing entity has given written notice as provided in subsection (5) specifying the purpose or project for which the moneys will in fact be applied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the borrowing entity has given written notice as provided in subsection (5), specifying the purpose or project for which the moneys will in fact be applied by the borrowing entity, this section applies and has effect as if"

§ `s 271: liability of trustees for debenture holders`

-- src:42613 | (2) Subsection (1) does not invalidate —
-- src:42615 | (a) any release otherwise validly given in respect of anything
-- src:42616 | done or omitted to be done by a trustee before the giving of
-- src:42617 | the release; or
-- src:42619 | (b) any provision enabling such a release to be given —
-- src:42621 | (i) on the agreement thereto of a majority of not less
-- src:42622 | than three fourths in nominal value of the debenture
-- src:42623 | holders present and voting in person or, where
-- src:42624 | proxies are permitted, by proxy at a meeting
-- src:42625 | summoned for the purpose; and
-- src:42630 | (ii) either with respect to specific acts or omissions or on
-- src:42631 | the dissolution of the trustee or on the trustee’s
-- src:42632 | ceasing to act.
@ref s 271(2) (src:42613-42632)
GIVEN
    `the release was otherwise validly given in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by the trustee before the release was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the release otherwise validly given, in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by the trustee before the giving of the release?
    `the provision enables such a release to be given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision enable such a release to be given?
    `the nominal value of the debenture holders who agree` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the debentures held by the holders who agree to the release, in Singapore dollars?
    `the nominal value of the debenture holders present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the debentures held by the holders present and voting in person (or, where proxies are permitted, by proxy) at the meeting summoned for the purpose, in Singapore dollars?
    `the release is with respect to specific acts or omissions, or on the dissolution of the trustee or its ceasing to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the release with respect to specific acts or omissions, or on the dissolution of the trustee or on the trustee's ceasing to act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 271(2) subsection (1) does not invalidate the release or the provision` MEANS
    IF `the release was otherwise validly given in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by the trustee before the release was given` OR (`the provision enables such a release to be given` AND ((`the nominal value of the debenture holders who agree` TIMES 4) AT LEAST (`the nominal value of the debenture holders present and voting` TIMES 3)) AND `the release is with respect to specific acts or omissions, or on the dissolution of the trustee or its ceasing to act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not invalidate — (a) any release otherwise validly given in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by a trustee before the giving of the release; or (b) any provision enabling such a release to be given"
    -- "A majority of not less than three fourths in nominal value" is read as the agreeing nominal value being at least three fourths of the nominal value present and voting.

-- src:42634 | (3) Subsection (1) does not operate —
-- src:42636 | (a) to invalidate any provision in force on 29 December 1967
-- src:42637 | so long as any trustee then entitled to the benefit of that
-- src:42638 | provision remains a trustee of the deed in question; or
-- src:42640 | (b) to deprive any trustee of any exemption or right to be
-- src:42641 | indemnified in respect of anything done or omitted to be
-- src:42642 | done by the trustee while any such provision was in force.
@ref s 271(3) (src:42634-42642)
GIVEN
    `the provision was in force on 29 December 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the provision in force on 29 December 1967?
    `a trustee then entitled to the benefit of the provision remains a trustee of the deed in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a trustee who was then entitled to the benefit of the provision remain a trustee of the deed in question?
    `the trustee had an exemption or right to be indemnified in respect of anything done or omitted to be done while the provision was in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the trustee have an exemption or a right to be indemnified in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by the trustee while the provision was in force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 271(3) subsection (1) does not operate against the provision or the trustee's exemption` MEANS
    IF (`the provision was in force on 29 December 1967` AND `a trustee then entitled to the benefit of the provision remains a trustee of the deed in question`) OR `the trustee had an exemption or right to be indemnified in respect of anything done or omitted to be done while the provision was in force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not operate — (a) to invalidate any provision in force on 29 December 1967 so long as any trustee then entitled to the benefit of that provision remains a trustee of the deed in question"

-- src:42605 | 271.—(1) Subject to this section, any provision contained in a trust
-- src:42606 | deed relating to or securing an issue of debentures, or in any contract
-- src:42607 | with the holders of debentures secured by a trust deed, is void insofar
-- src:42608 | as it would have the effect of exempting a trustee thereof from or
-- src:42609 | indemnifying the trustee against liability for breach of trust where the
-- src:42610 | trustee fails to show the degree of care and diligence required as
-- src:42611 | trustee.
@ref s 271(1) (src:42605-42611)
GIVEN
    `the provision is contained in a trust deed relating to or securing an issue of debentures, or in a contract with the holders of debentures secured by a trust deed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision contained in a trust deed relating to or securing an issue of debentures, or in a contract with the holders of debentures secured by a trust deed?
    `the provision would have the effect of exempting the trustee from, or indemnifying the trustee against, liability for breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the provision have the effect of exempting the trustee from, or indemnifying the trustee against, liability for breach of trust?
    `the trustee fails to show the degree of care and diligence required as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee fail to show the degree of care and diligence required as trustee?
    `subsection (1) does not invalidate the release or the provision under subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 271(2) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `subsection (1) does not operate against the provision or the exemption under subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 271(3) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 271(1) the provision is void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`subsection (1) does not invalidate the release or the provision under subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`subsection (1) does not operate against the provision or the exemption under subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not invalidate — (a) any release otherwise validly given"
        IF `the provision is contained in a trust deed relating to or securing an issue of debentures, or in a contract with the holders of debentures secured by a trust deed` AND `the provision would have the effect of exempting the trustee from, or indemnifying the trustee against, liability for breach of trust` AND `the trustee fails to show the degree of care and diligence required as trustee`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void insofar as it would have the effect of exempting a trustee thereof from or indemnifying the trustee against liability for breach of trust where the trustee fails to show the degree of care and diligence required as trustee"
    -- FORK s271-1 | s 271(1) | `s 271(1) the provision is void` | took NOTHING where the provision is outside the limit "insofar as ... where the trustee fails to show the degree of care" and no carve-out applies | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {IN-SHORT} ("limits a grant or prohibition in its own wording ... and the case falls outside the limit"). The carve-outs of (2) and (3) are flat negatives ("does not invalidate"), so they give JUST FALSE.

§ `Subdivision (3): the duties as regulative rules`

-- The duties above with a named party and a named act, as regulative rules (PARTY ... MUST / SHANT ... WITHIN ... LEST BREACH).
-- The clock of every rule below is in DAYS from the event the text counts from. A rule that takes `the number of days allowed`
-- is given the days between that event and the last day the text allows, counted with sfa-periods (the tests show how).
-- A rule with no WITHIN is a duty the text gives no time limit: late performance is not a breach, so no trace of it
-- reaches BREACH; each is listed under "Rules with no breach path (sfad)" in NOTES.md.
-- Parties and acts carry no fields, so that no input is named inside an action (the stable binary reads such a name as a wildcard).

DECLARE `s 268 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 268 the prescribed entity`
    `s 268 the borrowing entity`
    `s 268 a guarantor entity`
    `s 268 the directors or equivalent persons`
    `s 268 the trustee for the holders of the debentures`

DECLARE `s 268 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 261(1C) comply with the condition or restriction`
    `s 265A(1) appoint a trustee for the holders of debentures for the entire tenure`
    `s 266(3)(b) apply to the court as the Authority directs`
    `s 266(4) apply to the court as the borrowing entity requests`
    `s 268(4)(a) provide the trustee in writing with the particulars of the charge`
    `s 268(4)(b) provide the trustee in writing with the particulars of the amounts advanced`
    `s 268(6)(a) lodge the half-year accounts with the trustee`
    `s 268(6)(b) lodge the annual accounts with the trustee`
    `s 268(9) lodge notice with the Authority that the accounts were not lodged`
    `s 268(11) lodge a copy of the trustee's notice with the Authority`
    `s 268A(1) prepare and make available a semi-annual report`
    `s 268A(2) lodge the semi-annual report with the trustee`
    `s 268A(3) lodge notice with the Authority that the report was not lodged`
    `s 268A(4) disclose the information to the holders`
    `s 268A(7) make the accounts available to the holders`
    `s 269(2) provide the information to the borrowing entity`
    `s 270(1) report to the trustee on the progress of the purpose or project`
    `s 270(3) lodge a copy of the notice with the Authority`
    `s 270(3) give written notice requiring repayment`
    `s 270(5) repay the moneys on demand`

-- src:41862 | and the prescribed entity must comply with every such condition or
-- src:41863 | restriction imposed on it by the Authority that has not been revoked
-- src:41864 | by the Authority.
@ref s 261(1C) (src:41862-41864)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 261(1C) the duty of a prescribed entity to comply with a condition or restriction` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the prescribed entity`
    MUST `s 261(1C) comply with the condition or restriction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the prescribed entity` BECAUSE "the prescribed entity did not comply with a condition or restriction imposed on it that has not been revoked"

-- src:41971 | 265A.—(1) Where an offer of debentures is made in or
-- src:41972 | accompanied by a prospectus, the borrowing entity must appoint a
-- src:41973 | trustee for the holders of debentures (called in this section the
-- src:41974 | appointed trustee) for the entire tenure of the debentures.
@ref s 265A(1) (src:41971-41974)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 265A(1) the duty to appoint a trustee for the holders of debentures` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the borrowing entity`
    MUST `s 265A(1) appoint a trustee for the holders of debentures for the entire tenure`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the borrowing entity` BECAUSE "no trustee was appointed for the holders of debentures for the entire tenure"

-- src:42127 | (b) may, and if the borrowing entity so requires, must direct
-- src:42128 | the trustee to apply to the court for an order under
-- src:42129 | subsection (5); and the trustee must apply accordingly.
@ref s 266(3)(b) (src:42127-42129)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 266(3)(b) the duty of the trustee to apply to the court as directed` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the trustee for the holders of the debentures`
    MUST `s 266(3)(b) apply to the court as the Authority directs`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the trustee for the holders of the debentures` BECAUSE "the trustee did not apply to the court as the Authority directed"

-- src:42143 | the trustee may, and where the borrowing entity has requested the
-- src:42144 | trustee to do so, must apply to the court for an order under
-- src:42145 | subsection (5).
@ref s 266(4) (src:42143-42145)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 266(4) the duty of the trustee to apply to the court on the request of the borrowing entity` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the trustee for the holders of the debentures`
    MUST `s 266(4) apply to the court as the borrowing entity requests`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the trustee for the holders of the debentures` BECAUSE "the trustee did not apply to the court when the borrowing entity requested it to"

-- src:42261 | (a) in writing provide the trustee, within 21 days after the
-- src:42262 | creation of the charge, with the particulars of any charge
-- src:42263 | created by the entity or the guarantor entity, as the case
-- src:42264 | requires; and
@ref s 268(4)(a) (src:42261-42264)
GIVEN
    `the entity` IS A `s 268 party` @desc Which entity must provide the particulars: the borrowing entity or a guarantor entity?
    `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the creation of the charge may the particulars be provided? (The text allows 21.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 268(4)(a) the duty to provide the trustee with particulars of the charge within 21 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the entity`
    MUST `s 268(4)(a) provide the trustee in writing with the particulars of the charge`
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the entity` BECAUSE "the particulars of the charge were not provided to the trustee within 21 days after its creation"

-- src:42266 | (b) when the amount to be advanced on the security of the
-- src:42267 | charge is indeterminate, in writing provide the trustee,
-- src:42268 | within 7 days after the advance, with particulars of the
-- src:42269 | amount or amounts in fact advanced.
@ref s 268(4)(b) (src:42266-42269)
GIVEN
    `the entity` IS A `s 268 party` @desc Which entity must provide the particulars: the borrowing entity or a guarantor entity?
    `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the advance may the particulars be provided? (The text allows 7.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 268(4)(b) the duty to provide the trustee with particulars of the amounts advanced within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the entity`
    MUST `s 268(4)(b) provide the trustee in writing with the particulars of the amounts advanced`
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the entity` BECAUSE "the particulars of the amounts advanced were not provided to the trustee within 7 days after the advance"

-- src:42280 | (a) a profit and loss account for the first 6 months of every
-- src:42281 | financial year of the entity and a balance sheet as at the end
-- src:42282 | of that period, not later than 3 months after the expiration
-- src:42283 | of the period of 6 months; and
@ref s 268(6)(a) (src:42280-42283)
GIVEN
    `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the end of the first 6 months of the financial year may the accounts be lodged? (The text allows 3 months.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 268(6)(a) the duty to lodge the half-year accounts with the trustee within 3 months` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the directors or equivalent persons`
    MUST `s 268(6)(a) lodge the half-year accounts with the trustee`
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the directors or equivalent persons` BECAUSE "the half-year accounts were not lodged with the trustee not later than 3 months after the 6 months"

-- src:42285 | (b) a profit and loss account for every financial year of the
-- src:42286 | entity and a balance sheet as at the end of that period, not
-- src:42287 | later than 5 months after the expiration of that financial
-- src:42288 | year.
@ref s 268(6)(b) (src:42285-42288)
GIVEN
    `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the end of the financial year may the accounts be lodged? (The text allows 5 months.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 268(6)(b) the duty to lodge the annual accounts with the trustee within 5 months` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the directors or equivalent persons`
    MUST `s 268(6)(b) lodge the annual accounts with the trustee`
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the directors or equivalent persons` BECAUSE "the annual accounts were not lodged with the trustee not later than 5 months after the financial year"

-- src:42326 | (9) Where the directors or equivalent persons of a borrowing entity,
-- src:42327 | or the directors or equivalent persons of a guarantor entity, do not
-- src:42328 | lodge with the trustee the profit and loss accounts and balance sheets
-- src:42329 | as required under subsection (6) within the time prescribed under that
