`s 268A(3) the duty of the trustee to lodge notice with the Authority` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the trustee for the holders of the debentures`
    MUST `s 268A(3) lodge notice with the Authority that the report was not lodged`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the trustee for the holders of the debentures` BECAUSE "the trustee did not lodge notice with the Authority"
    -- FORK s268A-3i | s 268A(3) | `s 268A(3) the duty of the trustee to lodge notice with the Authority` | took "immediately" as a promptness standard with no number of days or hours the clock can count, so the rule has no WITHIN and no breach path | other reading WITHIN 0 (the same day), under which a trace one day late reaches BREACH | licence {CC} (a bare "must" not done, decided on the text's own words)

-- src:42415 | (4) A borrowing entity must immediately disclose, in such form and
-- src:42416 | manner as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under
-- src:42417 | section 341, to holders of unlisted debentures any information which
-- src:42418 | may materially affect —
-- src:42420 | (a) the risks and returns of the unlisted debentures; or
-- src:42422 | (b) the price or value of the unlisted debentures.
@ref s 268A(4) (src:42415-42422)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 268A(4) the duty to disclose information materially affecting the unlisted debentures` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the borrowing entity`
    MUST `s 268A(4) disclose the information to the holders`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the borrowing entity` BECAUSE "the information was not disclosed to the holders of the unlisted debentures"
    -- FORK s268A-4i | s 268A(4) | `s 268A(4) the duty to disclose information materially affecting the unlisted debentures` | took "immediately" as a promptness standard with no number of days or hours the clock can count, so the rule has no WITHIN and no breach path | other reading WITHIN 0 (the same day), under which a trace one day late reaches BREACH | licence {CC} (a bare "must" not done, decided on the text's own words)

-- src:42460 | (7) A borrowing entity must ensure that each profit and loss account
-- src:42461 | or balance sheet that its directors or equivalent persons are required to
-- src:42462 | lodge under section 268(6) is made available, in such form and
-- src:42463 | manner as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under
-- src:42464 | section 341, to holders of unlisted debentures, on the day of lodgment
-- src:42465 | of the profit and loss account or balance sheet (as the case may be)
-- src:42466 | with the trustee for the holders of the unlisted debentures.
@ref s 268A(7) (src:42460-42466)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 268A(7) the duty to make the accounts available to the holders on the day of lodgment` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the borrowing entity`
    MUST `s 268A(7) make the accounts available to the holders`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the borrowing entity` BECAUSE "the accounts were not made available to the holders on the day they were lodged with the trustee"
    -- WITHIN 0: the clock starts on the day of lodgment with the trustee; "on the day of lodgment" is the same day.

-- src:42505 | (2) The guarantor entity must provide the borrowing entity with the
-- src:42506 | information required under subsection (1) before such date, being a
-- src:42507 | date not earlier than 14 days after the notice is given, as may be
-- src:42508 | specified in that behalf in the notice.
@ref s 269(2) (src:42505-42508)
GIVEN
    `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the notice is given may the information be provided? (The day before the date the notice specifies.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 269(2) the duty of the guarantor entity to provide the information before the specified date` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 a guarantor entity`
    MUST `s 269(2) provide the information to the borrowing entity`
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 a guarantor entity` BECAUSE "the information was not provided before the date specified in the notice"

-- src:42521 | 270.—(1) Where there is, in any prospectus issued in connection
-- src:42522 | with an offer of debentures, a statement as to any particular purpose
-- src:42523 | or project for which the moneys received by the borrowing entity in
-- src:42524 | response to the offer are to be applied, the borrowing entity must,
-- src:42525 | where there is a trustee for the holders of those debentures, from time
-- src:42526 | to time make reports to the trustee as to the progress that has been
-- src:42527 | made towards achieving such purpose or completing such project.
@ref s 270(1) (src:42521-42527)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 270(1) the duty to make reports to the trustee on progress` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the borrowing entity`
    MUST `s 270(1) report to the trustee on the progress of the purpose or project`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the borrowing entity` BECAUSE "no report on progress was made to the trustee"

-- src:42544 | the trustee may and, if in the trustee’s opinion it is necessary for the
-- src:42545 | protection of the interests of the holders of the debentures, must give
-- src:42546 | written notice to the borrowing entity requiring it to repay the moneys
-- src:42547 | so received by the borrowing entity and, within one month after such
-- src:42548 | notice is given, lodge with the Authority a copy thereof.
@ref s 270(3) (src:42544-42548)
GIVEN
    `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the notice is given may the copy be lodged with the Authority? (The text allows one month.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 270(3) the duty of the trustee to lodge a copy of the notice within one month` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the trustee for the holders of the debentures`
    MUST `s 270(3) lodge a copy of the notice with the Authority`
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the trustee for the holders of the debentures` BECAUSE "a copy of the notice was not lodged with the Authority within one month after the notice was given"

-- src:42550 | (4) The trustee must not give notice under subsection (3) if the
-- src:42551 | trustee is satisfied —
@ref s 270(4) (src:42550-42551)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 270(4) the bar on the trustee giving notice` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the trustee for the holders of the debentures`
    SHANT `s 270(3) give written notice requiring repayment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the trustee for the holders of the debentures` BECAUSE "the trustee gave notice under subsection (3) when satisfied of a matter in subsection (4)"

-- src:42566 | (5) Upon receipt by the borrowing entity of a notice referred to in
-- src:42567 | subsection (3), the borrowing entity is liable to repay, and on demand
-- src:42568 | in writing by a person entitled thereto must immediately repay to the
-- src:42569 | person any moneys owing to the person as the result of a loan or
-- src:42570 | deposit made in response to the offer unless —
@ref s 270(5) (src:42566-42570)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 268 party` `s 268 act`
`s 270(5) the duty of the borrowing entity to repay the moneys on demand` MEANS
    PARTY `s 268 the borrowing entity`
    MUST `s 270(5) repay the moneys on demand`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 268 the borrowing entity` BECAUSE "the borrowing entity did not repay the moneys on demand"
    -- FORK s270-5i | s 270(5) | `s 270(5) the duty of the borrowing entity to repay the moneys on demand` | took "on demand in writing ... must immediately repay" as a promptness standard with no number of days or hours the clock can count, so the rule has no WITHIN and no breach path | other reading WITHIN 0 (the same day), under which a trace one day late reaches BREACH | licence {CC} (a bare "must" not done, decided on the text's own words)
